- **S8 close.** Cael speaks the rough four-year line and question; Karis answers both other speeches (`source ch8:105–113`). Fix 6 restores the complete protected close. The source staging at the foot of the stair is not imported into the loft.
- **Cleon marker.** Cleon says “Off floors,” Karis supplies the full three-floor/fifty-two-sheet answer, and Cleon repeats “Fifty-two sheets” (`source ch9:11–15`). Fix 7 restores that whole exchange.
- **S9 hand exchange.** Lira says “Four hands,” Cael answers “Four,” and Lira says “Right” after the ladder fails to pull (`source ch9:67–87`; `BOOK_MAP:399`). The current marker is wrongly left after the clerk writes four (`ch26:215–217`). Fix 9 inserts the protected exchange at Lira's completed ladder beat; fix 10 removes the later marker.

The source's full refusal paragraph cannot be restored: it gives Vastin an age, repeats a numeric span and makes the earlier reading history incompatible with the edition's closed Books 5–6 (`source ch7:89`; `OWNER-DECISIONS:24–25`; `book-05 ch58:229`; `book-06 ch40:197–213`). The map deliberately protects only `I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why.` (`BOOK_MAP:398`; `ch21:121`). The necessary edition-specific reconciliation is therefore fix 4, not the source paragraph.

## 6. New canon minted

Rulings follow the AUTHOR-REPORT list (`AUTHOR-REPORT:78–95`).

- **KEEP:** Line at the river and the one-half lifting of the road hold (`ch20:3–31`); the nine/six/three wayposts and pull-in (`ch20:41–49,137–143`; `ch21:3–11`); bridge construction and five piers (`ch22:9–57`); the outer gate's bead/head count (`ch22:59–73`); tier rights, cards, coat colours and the sick-house board (`ch22:87–113`; `ch23:77–105`; `ch25:145–171,207–219`); outer-district boards, rope-walk, trough, landing and traffic rules (`ch22:87–151`; `ch23:107–125`); the two forges (`ch22:153–179`); the two-door inn and week price (`ch22:181–209`); Seln's load route and cut (`ch24:233–257`; `ch25:225–263`; `ch26:3–133`); the cook-house (`ch24:45–65`); Karis as unnamed bearer and the provision fields (`ch23:253–275`; `ch24:145–151,221–225`); the quarry report (`ch23:245–269`); the registry back, unnamed clerk, dark stone and inward-opening door (`ch26:131–275`); Oryn's two-gate circuit, crooked wrist and live birth (`ch22:215–283`; `ch25:3–83`); the small objects and unnamed roles (`ch21:13–17`; `ch22:195–205`; `ch24:207–217`; `ch25:185–219`). None contradicts BOOK_MAP items 16–18 or later packets (`BOOK_MAP:68–73`; `MOVEMENT-005:26–44`).
- **AMEND:** Vastin's refusal weighting at `ch21:147` by fix 4, for the closed Book 6 reason above. The request and refusal chronology, file anchors, flat plate, nine-thousand figure, papers and four certifications otherwise agree with Books 5–6 (`book-05 ch58:199,229`; `book-06 ch14:53–65,132–144`; `book-06 ch40:197–213`; `book-06 ch49:201–209`; `ch21:91–145,189–197`; `ch23:39–55,183–225`).
- **AMEND:** Cleon's lamp term only (`ch24:163`) by fix 8 so the already-lit end of Movement 5's middle gallery remains possible (`MOVEMENT-005:26`). His appearance, counter terms, no-look at Cael and step-late stop stay (`ch24:51–59,127–193`).
- **CUT:** none of the listed inventions. The gatepost is a trial rather than a use; the child's distant counting does not imply a Kindling; and the iron-door blocking is source-different staging that the plan leaves to the author (`ch20:199–209`; `ch26:21–25,245–275`).

## 7. Names

No unapproved person, place or animal name is minted. Treswick, Oxhollow, Ostrand, Lowmarch, Millrace and Cleon are plan/canon names; the brown mule remains unnamed. The clerk, keepers, innkeeper, porters, carters, smiths, cook-house boy, Oryn's patients and both unnamed holds remain roles (`ch22:59–73,181–209,215–283`; `ch23:77–105,237–275`; `ch24:45–49`; `ch25:3–83`; `ch26:147–219`). `Cael did not learn his name ... on any day after it` keeps the clerk unnamed rather than naming him (`ch26:185`); it is an unnecessary future lock but agrees with the owner's explicit “do not name” instruction (`MOVEMENT-004:8,62`), so it is not a repair finding.

## 8. Next-movement inheritance

Movement 5's packet carries the M3 baseline and its own 284th opening, but not the following surviving M4 particulars. Its author must inherit all of them:

- **Who is below.** Inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with Cleon at the stair head; the unnamed clerk and his lantern remain outside. Seln is above ground, not on the 284th card or count, positioned to see who comes to the door. Oryn and the brown mule are at the second unnamed gate north (`ch25:87–117`; `ch26:183–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT:101`).
- **Loads and papers.** Boxes remain on Brom, Lira and Cael; the kit case remains on Vastin; Karis has the flat, hide/calfskin, copied page in oilcloth, dead surveyor's ledger and notebook. The fifty-two first copies are back in their box in order; Oryn's bowl is under Brom's lashing; Seln retains his closed case; Cleon has the two-cornered card (`ch24:199–225,275–293`; `ch25:89–117,229–237`; `ch26:195,213,261–267`; inherited M3 custody at `STATE_LEDGER:306–308`).
- **What Cleon has seen and been told.** He has seen one drawn sheet from fused, grey, joinless floors; he knows there are three places and fifty-two sheets; he has been told they are older than what the Compact found, but not Karis's theory, purpose or proposed meaning. He has not noticed Cael. His terms are all sheets in order, brought below, no theory before he looks, his carried lamp under his control, no other carried light or fire (`ch24:65–181` after fixes 7–8).
- **Inn.** The six—Cael, Brom, Lira, Karis, Seln and Vastin—have the warm long loft over the stable for a week from the 282nd, with the pot at dusk and seven bowls; the street door is for names and the yard half-door takes money without writing (`ch22:181–209`; `ch23:3–57,227–233`). Price paid: two marks. Purse: 136 (`ch22:195–199`; `ch24:265`).
- **Count and restriction.** Karis is the unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands. Seln is not on the 284th count. Both upper keepers counted the card; the yard clerk asked nothing and wrote *four*. None of the four restricted names has been written, so the asset-restriction remains pending (`ch25:97–117,145–171,225–247`; `ch26:183–223`; `book-06 ch58:49–53`).
- **Day and bodies.** It is the forenoon of the 284th. Vastin's right knee is day five of thirty, still stiff, with stick/no kneeling/no running/no wall; he has now sat three times and descended twenty-two steps, catching one slip with his left hand. Brom has five days left on the two right toes and the older shoulder knot; Lira's arm is day nineteen out of wool and has carried the box with both arms. Cael is sound apart from the box strap (`ch25:87,197–205`; `ch26:47–127,153`; `AUTHOR-REPORT:103,105,107,113`).
- **Cael's state.** Ten fragments; deployment thirty-two. He has made the fourth and fifth self-readings, both around/not in, and concluded that Tide reports only current and cannot read the still place. He owes Oryn an admission at Millrace. Lira has read the log. The square/steps/crown promise still holds and has now cost him something (`ch20:95–215`; `ch21:49–65,227–247`; `ch26:9–25,175`).
- **Vastin and Cael.** Vastin has confessed both the sound institutional reason for refusing certification and his private relief at not learning what another plate would say. Cael has given him the fact of two self-readings and the instrument's limit, but not what reads, fragments, mechanism, date or arithmetic. Each holds one fact from the other; the relationship is explicitly ground, not friendship (`ch21:121–223` after fix 4).
- **Other live state.** Lira's Iron-first paper remains unshown; the ladder no longer pulls. Karis has recognized the bridge's dark stone under the registry and has not yet stated a conclusion. The sixty yards of four-strand remain owed and Brom intends to buy them going out. Oryn has delivered a live daughter, is spent and a day behind her circuit, has heard of no leaf, and still owes Cael the reading (`ch22:125–127,215–283`; `ch24:219–231`; `ch25:3–83`; `ch26:47–79,137–145`).

