    31	"The man below counts, since feet are all that he is asked for; the men above do not count those who come by right. They read. A certificate is a name, and the district that issued it, and a number, and it is entered at the gate, with the hour, and goes up to a counter before night to be laid against a list." He did not raise his voice. "There are four names in this loft which must not be written in any book inside that wall. I told you why on the ninth day, and a man who used to certify such papers told you again at a board. One hour is what the paper allows; you would not be at the third gate before it was served."
    32	
