editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:4361:- **Injuries, as fixed on the page:** Lira, left forearm bitten through between wrist and elbow, held about thirty counts, never shaken; mended in an hour at the line; eight small pink marks; slung in a strip of Thornwater's blanket, the hand under the opposite collarbone. Right ankle over outward a third time; taped on the 97th; flat-footed, whole sole. Karis, throat pressed by her own fists under the jaws; knuckles skinned; no voice on the 96th–97th; a croak on the 98th; single rasped words on the 99th. Brom, a straight cut across the pads of four fingers of ONE hand [corrected at close: the protected unit gives one hand, four finger-pads]; mended at noon on the 97th; nothing drawn until the hundredth. Cael, left calf opened along the old seam on a stone in the rut; bound by Karis in a blanket strip that stayed on until Thornwater's yard on the 99th (never bound or mended by Oryn) [corrected at close]; counting eleven strides on the 97th, about forty by the evening of the 98th, none by noon of the 99th; a pale seam "four days, counting the one it went on". Left forearm struck in the second lock; dead to the elbow that night; back to the wrist on the 99th. Ribs: the tape off in the yard on the 99th. Seln: nothing. Oryn: spent to the bottom on the 96th; two mendings at noon on the 97th; none on the 98th or 99th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:4390:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. Three mendings on the crew in two days; none since. She has crossed the line eight times alone at dawn on the 98th, which only Cael saw. She has read him five times at the surface and once at depth, and has found movement, "more than one", and no banks. She felt something change in him in the twentieth minute; she has been told that he did it and that he must tell her what he is; **she does not know the mechanism**. Thornwater's bench is owed four days and is put off until after noon.
