editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3168:- **Road times (prose, fixed):** Lowmarch ↔ Thornwater two days; Thornwater → the Fallow rise two days; Lowmarch → Oxhollow six days (north-west); Lowmarch → Millrace one day south on the Stair road; Millrace's fork → the Stair's line the same afternoon; the Stair → the Hall three days along the bearing; the Hall → the fork one day; the fork → the fourth site a day and a half; the fourth site → Lowmarch six days; the fourth site's gap → Thornwater four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3506:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`) and the coordinator's ten audit fixes. Facts changed: Teague knows only that the healer was late, not why, and cannot set his lost day against the five; Brom's older ash wedge was not lost and lies with the three boxes; Oryn's sum now reads whole on the 99th, the long reading on the 100th at the earliest, four days of work at Thornwater's table beyond her stop and one day put on the route; Seln asks leave to go ahead and leaves scratched pebbles for word, and finds a clawless footmark at the first seep; Oryn washes her hands before she kneels, and checks her hands on Brom's wrist in the middle of the first reading; the ankle is asked for from the mule's back on the morning of the 82nd; chapter 18 has three scenes. Word counts, metrics, line numbers and flags elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the movement now stands at 41,346 words.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3512:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3522:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken". **Her sum (her window, the 92nd):** whole on the 99th by the rule, though her hands say sooner; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; her Thornwater stop ends on the 95th; she means to work four days more at Thornwater's table and has put one day on the route, for the reading. She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record. She told Teague on the hill only that she was late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3548:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the ten audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (three more lines in Teague's window changed so he cannot tie the healer's lateness to the five); six tracked passages restaged; about 1,480 words of repeated survey procedure removed; orienting sentences at the split; the day-80 log reads "Some of the herd went over the edge after the cart. How many: heard, not sworn…"; a day-84 reset at Teague's window; Oryn's sum reconciled (whole on the 99th; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; a plan of four days at Thornwater's table plus one added day, which she changes at Thornwater's gate on the 93rd). New: Seln reads a heavy clawless footmark at a seep (unidentified sign; KEEP). Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — one applied (ch16: Seln shows the width with his hands). All six tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 28 protected. 41439 words. Coordinator correction logged: the Bodies bullet first mis-stated whose leg was mended; corrected above and the Movement 4 author told.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3574:- **The two HOLD slips (flag):** one bark and one shingle; a bull to be brought down off top grazing before the snow, and a ford to be staked. Each hold "asked who". They will wait a fortnight for the five and then have Teague. Cael tells Pike on the 91st not to keep them past the fortnight. **They are still on the oak at the end of the movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3600:**Calendar.** Sunset on the **ninety-sixth day past the Line**, at the eastern lip of the Fallow Ring's floor. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term"; "frost"; "before the snow"; "fortnight"). Days on the page: 84 (dusk), 85, 86, 87, 88, 89, 90, 91, 92, 93, 94, 95, 96; and, in Teague's window, the evening of the 89th. Weather: frost every morning; dry roads; a north wind on the Fallow. The next movement opens where this one stops.
