editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/source-tracking.stdout.log:3198:   193	*Under the rule: the rule is not for the days I want to. It's for the days I don't notice I've started. She read me for twenty minutes with my leave and could not find a bank. I could read her in twenty and find every bank she has, and she has walked past that line eleven times without stepping off the road and stepped over it eight times alone in the dark, and she is going north at first light with a route seventeen days late and my rule in her pocket. Every time. Written where the inventory goes, so that it gets read every time the inventory does.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/source-tracking.stdout.log:3495:   277	She had crossed it eight times in the grey, where nobody was to see, and one person had seen and held his tongue for twelve days. She had gone in with her palms up, and with two fingers on her own wrist, and backward, and with her eyes shut; and she had stood in it for a count of a hundred with her arms hanging. Each time it had been the same. On one side of a grey stone she was a Tide, Iron, of the fourth rank, with a reserve like a purse. On the other she was a woman in a dead man's coat who could tie a knot.
