editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/source-tracking.stdout.log:4768:    49	- **The first self-reading:** on his back in the loft, two fingers on his own wrist and a palm on the breastbone. Written above everything: ten flows and no banks, a limit of the reading. Then a place near the middle that none of the ten runs through: it is not a current, not the tenth, not one of the nine; everything is nearer there; the ten go round it. Three things he can count: where; that nothing in it moves; that all ten go round it and none through. **It is not named.** He tells nobody what he found; he tells Lira and the six only that there is a thing and that it is the healer's to hear first.
