editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-001/compiled-prompt.md:1339:- **Road times (prose, fixed):** Lowmarch ↔ Thornwater two days; Thornwater → the Fallow rise two days; Lowmarch → Oxhollow six days (north-west); Lowmarch → Millrace one day south on the Stair road; Millrace's fork → the Stair's line the same afternoon; the Stair → the Hall three days along the bearing; the Hall → the fork one day; the fork → the fourth site a day and a half; the fourth site → Lowmarch six days; the fourth site's gap → Thornwater four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-42.md:119:"There's a child. You told us about a child with a chest. I can keep it still for four days; I've kept it still for ten."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:247:He had come back the night before from the river stations by the post road. He had walked all six in four days. Every frame was sound, though one had been shimmed and would read the damp no longer, and he had written that it would read the damp no longer, and signed it. His left hand had disliked the mornings on the river very much. His clerk had had a fire lit in the room before he came in, without being asked, which the clerk did perhaps twice a year, and had said nothing about it.
