editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:3539:   213	That was the whole of it. Five words had gone out from a desk by a noon dispatch, after a man had weighed them for four days on a post road and found them worth sending though they would stop nothing. They had stopped nothing. They were in the minute as an absence, between the count of the exhibits and the count of the orders, and the clerk was already reading the next line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:3811:     5	"Call days," she said. "Four of them, before any ruling. In those four days a seat may recall a party to put a question it has thought of late, and so may its evaluation seat, and the code gives them an hour's notice to do it in. An hour, on foot, from wherever the party is lodged." She looked out at the switchbacks. "That was a fair rule when every respondent lived over his own shop in the town. It was not written with a bluff in mind. Your hill is an hour and a quarter from that room by a good horse, and so for four days the house must live where it can hear the exchange's bell. The code calls it keeping within the bell. I have always thought it rather a handsome phrase for a nuisance."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:3815:     9	"In my time? Twice. Once to ask a guild master his mother's maiden name, which had been left off a form." The counsel's mouth moved at one corner. "Seats do not think of things late. They are very thorough about thinking of them early. But the rule stands, and we keep it, and in four days nobody will be able to say that the house was not where it was told to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:4344:   239	She got in. For a moment, before the door shut, he saw her face with nobody looking at it, and it was the face of a woman who has known a thing for four days and is not going to say it in a stable yard. He did not understand that then, and put it away to look at later.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:4770:    17	"*Resigned in good standing.*" She said it without surprise. "I know the door. I have known it for four days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:4806:    53	"So I kept it," she said. "For four days, through a return and a ruling. I let you hear the hood say *revoked* without knowing how short the time was. I should like to say that it was easy and that I never wavered, and I can't; I sat in a carriage this afternoon and very nearly said it through the window." Her mouth moved a little. "I wanted it to be yours. If you went, I wanted you to go because you had priced it with your own people, at a table, with my need left out of the sum. And if you stayed, I meant to walk beside you into that frame-house and take what they wrote."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:4812:    59	He found that he could not answer. He had been keeping the largest thing he knew from her for half a year, and it had sat between them like a lie in every room; she had kept a thing from him for four days, and he saw now which of the two silences had been the kinder.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:5490:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22:| 7 | Corridor | 5,438 | 5 | **Paragraph nine:** Bracken knows *evaluation integrity* from his own filing (an Ostrand frame reading Stones a rank high); the counsel's twelve sections, never before turned on a person; "I'm the frame." / "A frame that will not read true comes off the floor." Remedy, paragraph 34. The counsel: "A count is evidence. Indignation never was." **Chapter fourteen** in Bracken's flattest voice (Tier B); "Somebody… imagined you." **Withrow's morning after**: the ferry pass, the guild hall, the sealed file, the house's letter; **"It's expulsion that follows you."**; the two restrictions and the daughter at her counter every week for a year. **Bracken's pocket calendar:** dated the first day, served the eighth, seven days at a walk ("sent to be watched getting here"), **due the twenty-second**; *respondent made default*. **Karis's six slips**; **"It's not a question. It's a corridor. Every door in it is real law, and every door opens one way."**; "The house will answer"; *fled*; four days. **The stratum note, sideways:** "They're trying to move him back inside the instrument." / "I don't know why that distinction feels important. Noting it." A question mark in Cael's notebook. **The residence awake for her:** Seln's lamp in the wing; Brom's tea kept hot for hours, four cups; Karis counts the room; "Thank you for the tea." Cael tells it; **Brom: "Corridor."**; **Lira: "What if the people didn't fail this time?"**; "Then there's a place where they read it wrong." **The first pole**, verbatim, in one pass; the records hall's lamps out in pairs; the copy on the sill, first page up, **waiting for better light** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:5504:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/recheck-r1.md:328:- Every ≥0.50 pair in ch5–7 is a protected, Tier B or packet line, except "I'll have bones on it in four days" (0.59) and "'Four days,' she said to the room" (0.64). Fix 20 re-cuts the second.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:5769:The binding shape is explicit in `BOOK_MAP.md:112`: “the ruling in the year's last month; the Line crossed after the year's close.” The last-month row says “Closing sittings; Ilsev; the ruling; the council; the last bout” (`BOOK_MAP.md:122`), followed by “Four days before the year's close → after the close” (`BOOK_MAP.md:123`). M8 enters in “The academic year's last month. Two closing sittings at Ostrand. Brom's review on the year's last Fifth-day” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:13`). M9 enters “The morning after the last bout, four days before the academic year's close” (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:13`) and must end after the Line (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36`).
