editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:6264:59:Between the two sittings there were four days, and the four days were their own kind of instruction.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.stdout.log:6266:61:The delegation stayed at Ostrand in the guesting-house on the cathedral street, because going back to the bluff and returning would have cost two days of coach. They ate together in the evenings. Karis worked; she had a supplemental submission to draft on a point the seal had raised, and she drafted it, and it was good, and she knew while she was drafting it that the seal had raised the point out of courtesy and would rule the other way. Brom found a yard behind the guesting-house and used it, one-handed at first and then with both, and Lira came down and worked opposite him on the second morning, on an ankle that had come out of its strapping two weeks before, and neither of them said anything about the four days or the ruling or the road.
