editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/plan-audit.stdout.log:3580:   558	- **Injuries, as fixed on the page:** Lira, left forearm bitten through between wrist and elbow, held about thirty counts, never shaken; mended in an hour at the line; eight small pink marks; slung in a strip of Thornwater's blanket, the hand under the opposite collarbone. Right ankle over outward a third time; taped on the 97th; flat-footed, whole sole. Karis, throat pressed by her own fists under the jaws; knuckles skinned; no voice on the 96th–97th; a croak on the 98th; single rasped words on the 99th. Brom, a straight cut across the pads of four fingers of ONE hand [corrected at close: the protected unit gives one hand, four finger-pads]; mended at noon on the 97th; nothing drawn until the hundredth. Cael, left calf opened along the old seam on a stone in the rut; bound by Karis in a blanket strip that stayed on until Thornwater's yard on the 99th (never bound or mended by Oryn) [corrected at close]; counting eleven strides on the 97th, about forty by the evening of the 98th, none by noon of the 99th; a pale seam "four days, counting the one it went on". Left forearm struck in the second lock; dead to the elbow that night; back to the wrist on the 99th. Ribs: the tape off in the yard on the 99th. Seln: nothing. Oryn: spent to the bottom on the 96th; two mendings at noon on the 97th; none on the 98th or 99th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/plan-audit.stdout.log:3609:   587	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. Three mendings on the crew in two days; none since. She has crossed the line eight times alone at dawn on the 98th, which only Cael saw. She has read him five times at the surface and once at depth, and has found movement, "more than one", and no banks. She felt something change in him in the twentieth minute; she has been told that he did it and that he must tell her what he is; **she does not know the mechanism**. Thornwater's bench is owed four days and is put off until after noon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/plan-audit.stdout.log:3703:    67	Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/plan-audit.stdout.log:3804:    49	- **The first self-reading:** on his back in the loft, two fingers on his own wrist and a palm on the breastbone. Written above everything: ten flows and no banks, a limit of the reading. Then a place near the middle that none of the ten runs through: it is not a current, not the tenth, not one of the nine; everything is nearer there; the ten go round it. Three things he can count: where; that nothing in it moves; that all ten go round it and none through. **It is not named.** He tells nobody what he found; he tells Lira and the six only that there is a thing and that it is the healer's to hear first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/plan-audit.stdout.log:4007:   117	- **The first self-reading (flag):** two fingers on his own wrist, a palm on the breastbone; at ten, his own gait; in the long one, ten flows and no banks; near the middle, where the ten lie closest, a place that every one of them goes round and none goes through; no sound in it; nothing moves. Three countable things. Not named.
