editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8581:   131	"Then it stays shut," said Brom. "We've walked four days for a line."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8795:    21	He got the trouser leg up and the binding off. The ford's line along the inside of the calf, opened on the rim's edge four days ago and washed and bound at the stone and not touched since, was a seam. Pink, closed its whole length, the black gone out of it. She put a thumb along it and pressed, and he did not move, and she pressed harder, and he did not move.
