editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6026:     3	The escort order's forensics took Seln four days, and he conducted them the way he conducted everything, in the margins of a working week, invisibly, from the service side, and what they returned was the last input the fifteen-year audit required.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6356:     5	The note came up from the assessment office at the seventh bell, on the counter's ordinary stock, in the counter's ordinary hand, addressed to the delegation's floor coordinator and copied nowhere: *Wing three practice allocation revised. Enrollee's supervised hours suspended four days pending recovery-of-form. Reallocation to follow.* It was a true document about a true thing and it said nothing whatever, and Cael read it lying flat on his back on the residence floor with his boots still on, because the floor was the only surface in the room that had stopped moving, and thought, with the part of him that was still able to draft sentences, that the man had built a postponement out of a scheduling instrument in under an hour and had probably not thought of it as difficult.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:7204:1. Semifinals the ninth (ch40 board line 13; ch42 line 3 "the ninth of Reaping") and the tenth (ch41 line 61, 83; ch43). 2. Deep hip strain, "clicked once, on the oil", four days off (ch42 lines 241–245); tallow casting-floor skill (ch42 line 191). 3. "Archmarshal Vastin" named at the reading (ch38 line 87); no age anywhere (grep "sixty|fifty-one": none). 4. Schedule on the page: sittings 12th–15th, facilities the 14th, observation the 20th (ch40 line 17). 5. Karis draws the three columns on her slate; the "they don't fight" insight and the Log are Cael's (ch43 lines 193–253). 6. Both vocabulary counts reported (AUTHOR-REPORT). 7. Gwen's aunt stays an anecdote (ch40 line 117). 8. The slip known only to Brom and Cael; the observer "turned a page and wrote on" (ch43 line 285). 9. Withrow's grain store (ch38 line 109). 10. Defense done in the days available; "six days" (ch42 line 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:7210:**Calendar.** Matches the pending ledger block day for day: d168 courier/reading (Third-day, unit at the sixth bell); d170 Fifth-day board; d172 Seventh-day (Seln's requisition, Lira's room "If I win tomorrow"); d173 the ninth (file closed at the second bell; Lira–Fiske at the fourth bell); d174 the tenth (Brom–Merrick; "Nine days"); d175 the eleventh (slip; Brom "Nine days from now … three hours"; "Three nights ago" the cross — d172, correct; "two days ago" Merrick on the stair — d172, correct); d176 the twelfth (arrival at the fourth bell; close "seven days … eight"). Gwen's "on Third-day" for the next unit = d175, consistent with the weekly Third-day unit. Seln's bundle "would wait four days" from d172 = d176. Lira's "nine days" is counted from the tenth, as the ruling allows; the hip will be ten days old at the final, as the coordinator noted for M8. No Sowing date, no month order, no Sowing→Reaping count (#35). "A month back" for session fifteen (d141→d173 = 32 days) is fair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8360:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-27-- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8554:books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-07.md-163-She loaded it herself, at the gate, with the sun going off the bench above the roofs. The roll under the strap; the panniers, which had carried a box for four days and now carried the kit. Lira, on two feet with a hand on the stockade, watched her and said nothing; Brom held the mule's lead while she tightened a girth and gave it back without being asked, and she said "Hm," to him, and it was thanks. It was not a leaving that had been arranged. It was a healer at the end of a stop.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-42.txt:185:There was no moon, and the cloud had not lifted in four days. Past the stable passage the dark came down like a sack, and Cael stood in it at the top of the farm track with the others breathing round him and could not see his own hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-07.md:355:He had no word to give them, for a man did not speak to a bottom line that had cost him nothing. If they were what four lines said, then the board would put them across his road before the snow, and there would be something to say then, and something to price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/pre-repair-r1/chapter-44.md:105:"North in the morning," Oryn said. It was not an answer to Karis; it was a fact about a route. "Oxhollow's seventeen days late and the old woman's knee doesn't care what's under a floor. I'll be on the road at first light and I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board." She looked at him. "Thornwater's on my route. You know where that is now."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/pre-repair-r1/chapter-44.md:277:She had crossed it eight times in the grey, where nobody was to see, and one person had seen and held his tongue for twelve days. She had gone in with her palms up, and with two fingers on her own wrist, and backward, and with her eyes shut; and she had stood in it for a count of a hundred with her arms hanging. Each time it had been the same. On one side of a grey stone she was a Tide, Iron, of the fourth rank, with a reserve like a purse. On the other she was a woman in a dead man's coat who could tie a knot.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1353:- **n291** "She had been over the Fallow's eleven strips for four days at a trestle in a barn",
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1354:  so that "I looked for it for four days" is plain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1575:   new: `"This one. It's not on the Ring. I looked for it for four days and it isn't on any upright. It's here, on every wall, and it's not in the courses with the rest — it's *between* them. On its own. Here." The pencil moved along the sheet to the next one, and the next. "And here. And here. I've paced the spacing because I pace things. It comes every — " she looked at the notebook, where she had written it, and read it out as a number she had checked twice — "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride. It recurs, on the wall, at the perimeter's radius."`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1691:- POV: Cael ≈29,900. **Teague cutaway ≈1,700** (days 117–120: following the crew's trail three days along a bearing he does not understand, the healer brought because a shoulder was mended once; sitting down beside the boy; the column). **Karis cutaway ≈2,000** (days 119–120 at the far fire: three copies, the ledger, the edge laid and moved; it ends exactly on the pencil stopping; no who or why). **Seln cutaway ≈1,600** (days 124–128, the road home: the ledger in his coat; giving it to Karis and not asking for it back). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,800** (day 122 to about 128: the gap north-west, four days, three weeks late; Thornwater; the old woman's knee; writing the letter, ending on its four lines).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1726:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:2041:- **Road times (prose, fixed):** Lowmarch ↔ Thornwater two days; Thornwater → the Fallow rise two days; Lowmarch → Oxhollow six days (north-west); Lowmarch → Millrace one day south on the Stair road; Millrace's fork → the Stair's line the same afternoon; the Stair → the Hall three days along the bearing; the Hall → the fork one day; the fork → the fourth site a day and a half; the fourth site → Lowmarch six days; the fourth site's gap → Thornwater four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:2202:- **The first self-reading (flag):** two fingers on his own wrist, a palm on the breastbone; at ten, his own gait; in the long one, ten flows and no banks; near the middle, where the ten lie closest, a place that every one of them goes round and none goes through; no sound in it; nothing moves. Three countable things. Not named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:2216:- **Oryn's lateness (flag):** nine late at Thornwater and eleven at the next on the 104th (meaning to go on the 106th); she stays to read the arm at the fortnight; "sixteen out of this gate… A round never gives a day back; it takes one." (the 110th, in the yard); "Oxhollow's seventeen days late and the old woman's knee doesn't care what's under a floor" (the loft, the protected line), and in her window the odd day is the old woman's knee and Oxhollow is the 121st. Her window: the child was last heard on the 89th, looked for on the 109th, and cannot be heard before the 126th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:2238:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. **She knows the mechanism** (told on the 100th, with the nine by Path). Her hands are whole. She has set: on himself first; she is the one he tells; ask, every time; three readings on three days and then all of it; nobody read on the road to find out whether he can. She has not said what she would have answered, and has not forgiven him. She read Lira's arm on the 106th and the 110th. **She has left her mule with the crew** and gone north on foot with one pannier and a spare rope, **sixteen days late out of Thornwater and seventeen at Oxhollow**, to take the next gate's beast. She has said that she goes north at first light, that Oxhollow is seventeen days late, that Thornwater is on her route, and "Don't go in without me." She has heard no theory, since nobody has offered one.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:2388:- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:2558:- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:2574:| The still place | Located (M6, unnamed); named as *the still place* (M8); read three times; "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment." | *source, before, primordial, recurrence* (Book 9's word); a Rune-like "shape with bones" (Book 8's); any theory, including Oryn's |
