editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9359:7. **Chapter 43 Cael/Karis parallel — RESOLVED.** The diff removes the three-paragraph barn chain beginning “Cael had put no question to her in four days,” including the explicit pairing of “two people in that barn”. The barn now ends their private exchange on his refusal to ask and her recognition of it (`chapter-43.md:107–111`). Cael's parallel appears much later, after the healer, mule, bow and gate-walk transitions: “Karis has a thing that she won't write. I've a thing that I won't write” (`chapter-43.md:301`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9650:Oryn's sum now states every needed term: the ribs break on day 78; twenty-one days makes Cael whole on day 99 by her rule; the deep reading can first run on day 100; her ordinary Thornwater stop would end on day 95; four intervening days can be honest table work; the reading day cannot, so `She put a day on the route.` The plan is consistent with the later packets **because it is her day-92 intention and is visibly changed at Thornwater's gate on day 93**. Movement 4 has her say `You're a stop. I've added you`, walk the Fallow road on days 94–95, and remain with the six through the Ring; Movement 5 returns them to Thornwater on day 99 and runs the deep reading on day 100. The BOOK_MAP table fixes those same days. Do **not** take the author's offered cut: removing the second half of `She took it out of the round` would erase the clean distinction between four days she initially counts as route work and the one day she knowingly adds, without improving downstream continuity.
