editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:10330:295:"This one. It's not on the Ring. I looked for it for four days and it isn't on any upright. It's here, on every wall, and it's not in the courses with the rest — it's *between* them. On its own. Here." The pencil moved along the sheet to the next one, and the next. "And here. And here. I've paced the spacing because I pace things. It comes every — " she looked at the notebook, where she had written it, and read it out as a number she had checked twice — "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride. It recurs, on the wall, at the perimeter's radius."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/recheck-r1.stdout.log:10388:   109	The healer did not answer at once. He saw her look at his right hand, where it hung, and then at her own wrist; and for the space of one breath there was the hunger in her face that he had seen at a ford and in a yard, when she had wanted to know a thing more than she wanted her supper. She put it by as he had seen her put it by before.
