editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-51.txt:231:She got in. For a moment, before the door shut, he saw her face with nobody looking at it, and it was the face of a woman who has known a thing for four days and is not going to say it in a stable yard. He did not understand that then, and put it away to look at later.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:1531:"The house will answer," said Karis. "Because the other choice has its own word in the docket, and the word is fled, and this house is named on that paper, and I won't have fled written anywhere near it while I live here." She swept the six slips into one hand and tucked them into the back of her notebook. "I'll have bones on it in four days. And when the seat reads it, the seat will go through it with a pen and find nothing to mark. If the end's already fixed, I still want our tracks in the record, every step of them exactly where the code says a step goes."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:1595:Cael told them the rest: the answer anyway, the four days, and last the thing Karis had said sideways with her pen still moving, that the paper did not want the clause at all. It wanted him back in front of a frame.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:1863:Karis came down to supper that night for the first time in four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:3235:Minute of the 40th: evaluation seat, to be called. Refusal of the 44th: fully constituted. Who sat down in those five chairs in four days, without asking this office for the file?
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:4171:Brom had come up behind them, slower. At the turn of the stair he stopped, and Cael, a step below, saw his right hand go to the left side of his coat, where the inside pocket was, and rest there over the cloth. There was a square cream envelope in that pocket with its dark red seal still whole. It had come up with the post four days ago, and he had turned it over once at the table and put it away unopened, and nobody had asked. Now an office in his own province kept an open book with a question in it about his family, and his grandmother could turn its pages whenever she liked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:4193:The brass came up from the coast at last, and it is a third dearer than last year and not as good, and the founder says it is nobody's fault, which I believe, because it never is. I have a surveyor's level on the bench that came back to me after thirty years. I made it for the man's father. The bubble has wandered a hair, and the son brought it in to be put right; and then, when I had it in pieces, he asked me to set it back the way it was, because his father laid out every boundary in the valley with it a hair wrong and the whole valley is built to agree with it now. I spent four days deciding. In the end I did as he asked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:4327:You were right to set the level back the way the son wanted it. A valley that agrees with itself is worth keeping agreed. You'll have known that before you spent the four days; you spent them to be sure.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:8893:"I'm not asking to be difficult," she said. "I'm asking because I sat on that bench last night and listened to you all read forty of them out, and I've been doing my drills in my head all day, and I can't make them go." She looked at the coats. "That seat down there runs on it, and so does the evaluation. Every sitting we go to, we're sitting in the room and answering it, and it's the thing in the case. They want to read you again. We know now what reads you." She pulled her coat closer. "My carters said the stamps stop four days east, loaded, or three days light. I've been carrying that in my pocket since the dairy. We could be past the last station by the Seventh-day after next if we left on the Seventh-day."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:9715:He had come back the night before from the river stations by the post road. He had walked all six in four days. Every frame was sound, though one had been shimmed and would read the damp no longer, and he had written that it would read the damp no longer, and signed it. His left hand had disliked the mornings on the river very much. His clerk had had a fire lit in the room before he came in, without being asked, which the clerk did perhaps twice a year, and had said nothing about it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:10231:There was no moon, and the cloud had not lifted in four days. Past the stable passage the dark came down like a sack, and Cael stood in it at the top of the farm track with the others breathing round him and could not see his own hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:10355:Lira was at her chalk at the south end with her back to the door. She had taped her own wrists but not the ankle, because the healer had said there was nothing left in it to tape, and she stood now with her weight even on both feet and her left arm tucked a little toward her ribs, from the old habit, and did not look round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:10509:She had started it in the dairy week. Not that night; the night after, when she could not sleep for thinking about three carters and a road with four days of stamps on it and then none. She had thought then, lying on her back in the dark, about what she actually owned. Not the program. The program was Rooke's, and the east hall was the house's, and the red book belonged to a river academy and was only lent. The figure on the steward's sheet was hers, but it was hers the way a room is yours when somebody else holds the key; it meant something because a hall's seal was on it, and it would go on meaning something exactly as far as that seal was honoured.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:10665:They had spent four days on that table of renewals, in the annex, at the start of the year. He had found the nine days himself, in his own old Log, and Karis had let him find them. And a man in a mended coat had just stood up before a hood and said that every line of it was right, and thrown away a piece of his own petition rather than leave an error standing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:11463:He knew what would be done with it. The code let a seat proceed upon its own authority where a certificate was withheld; he had cited that section himself, once, long ago, when a guild hall's assessor would not sign. His line would stop nothing. The sittings would sit, and the ruling would be read, and somewhere in a minute a clerk would enter that a thing usually present was not there. That was the whole of what he could do, and he had weighed it on a post road for four days and found that it was still worth doing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:12183:Five words had gone out from a desk by a noon dispatch, after a man had weighed them for four days on a post road and found them worth sending though they would stop nothing. They had stopped nothing. They were in the minute as an absence, between the count of the exhibits and the count of the orders, and the clerk was already reading the next line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:12235:"Call days," she said. "Four of them, before any ruling. In those four days a seat may recall a party to put a question it has thought of late, and so may its evaluation seat, and the code gives them an hour's notice to do it in. An hour, on foot, from wherever the party is lodged." She looked out at the switchbacks. "That was a fair rule when every respondent lived over his own shop in the town. It was not written with a bluff in mind. Your hill is an hour and a quarter from that room by a good horse, and so for four days the house must live where it can hear the exchange's bell. The code calls it keeping within the bell. I have always thought it rather a handsome phrase for a nuisance."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:12239:"In my time? Twice. Once to ask a guild master his mother's maiden name, which had been left off a form." The counsel's mouth moved at one corner. "Seats do not think of things late. They are very thorough about thinking of them early. But the rule stands, and we keep it, and in four days nobody will be able to say that the house was not where it was told to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:12755:She got in. For a moment, before the door shut, he saw her face with nobody looking at it, and it was the face of a woman who has known a thing for four days and is not going to say it in a stable yard. He did not understand that then, and put it away to look at later.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:13175:"Resigned in good standing." She said it without surprise. "I know the door. I have known it for four days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:13211:"So I kept it," she said. "For four days, through a return and a ruling. I let you hear the hood say revoked without knowing how short the time was. I should like to say that it was easy and that I never wavered, and I can't; I sat in a carriage this afternoon and very nearly said it through the window." Her mouth moved a little. "I wanted it to be yours. If you went, I wanted you to go because you had priced it with your own people, at a table, with my need left out of the sum. And if you stayed, I meant to walk beside you into that frame-house and take what they wrote."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:13217:He could not answer. He had been keeping the largest thing he knew from her for half a year, and it had sat between them like a lie in every room; she had kept a thing from him for four days, and he saw now which of the two silences had been the kinder.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:13936:"There is a margin. A margin belongs to the officer who takes the paper, and I have been thirteen years learning what one is for." Bracken laid the pen down. "Somebody will open this, some year. He will see a challenge, and a ruling, and a withdrawal inside the same week, and he will ask himself the natural question, which is whether the house put you out to save itself. He will be a careful man, I hope, and I should like him to find that the registrar was there, and looked at the clock, and wrote down what he saw." He paused. "The chancellor knew of this door four days before you did, and she did not say one word to you about it. I know what that cost, for I was the one she did not send. It ought to be written somewhere that nobody pushed."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:14720:He was not anywhere. A watcher's line had him on the east road, four days out, with a cart, and there was no line after that. Beyond the last station no district ran, and a restriction must run in a district; it wanted a counter to be served at, and a book to be written in. The code had foreseen that, as it foresaw most things. The clerk found the phrase in a schedule and wrote it at the instrument's foot.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:14862:"That's four days of a man at my back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:15106:By charter of the registry, this house being chartered: TIER VERIFICATION available at the district station, Ostrand, four days west. No station lies east of the river crossing, and the station at the ford is unstaffed. TRAVEL ENDORSEMENTS may be lodged at this house for forward transmission; allow twenty days. ENROLLMENT INQUIRIES by the same. The chartered rates of this house are posted within. Complaints of a chartered house lie to the district seat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:15162:The grey rider had come up closer than he had been in four days, perhaps eighty yards off. He was mounted again, and he rode up the last of the rise at a walk, and stopped at the pillar's foot on its western side, with the cob's nose level with the stone. He did not come past it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:15170:He looked at each of them in turn, as the elder coat had done at the road's foot, and at Seln a little longer than the rest, and his face did not change. It was a plain weathered face. He had stood by a milestone with a tin cup through a recess and eleven sittings, and he had ridden four days at their backs without once pretending to be anything else.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/The-Compact-s-Hand-Eleven-v4-Directors-Cut.txt:15566:He did not ask anybody. He went round the foot of the block, where the pine had been dropping dead limbs for longer than there had been a road, and gathered them up, and broke them across his knee and laid them small to large. He was quicker at it than he had been four days ago, and he had the fire's place chosen, in the lee of the stone, before the gelding was out of the shafts.
