editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/pre-repair-author/chapter-50.md:5:"Call days," she said. "Four of them, before any ruling. In those four days a seat may recall a party to put a question it has thought of late, and so may its evaluation seat, and the code gives them an hour's notice to do it in. An hour, on foot, from wherever the party is lodged." She looked out at the switchbacks. "That was a fair rule when every respondent lived over his own shop in the town. It was not written with a bluff in mind. Your hill is an hour and a quarter from that room by a good horse, and so for four days the house must live where it can hear the exchange's bell. The code calls it keeping within the bell. I have always thought it rather a handsome phrase for a nuisance."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/pre-repair-author/chapter-50.md:9:"In my time? Twice. Once to ask a guild master his mother's maiden name, which had been left off a form." The counsel's mouth moved at one corner. "Seats do not think of things late. They are very thorough about thinking of them early. But the rule stands, and we keep it, and in four days nobody will be able to say that the house was not where it was told to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-23.md:7:It was the start of something, and so he took the inventory, as he took it at the start of anything. Three ribs were broken on the left side, low; they had been taped on the eighty-first day, and the tape was to come off on the ninety-ninth and not before. The calf was bound in a healer's cloth and was closing by itself, as his hurts did. Lira had a shin that was four days old, and an ankle that no healer on this road was going to mend, and one boot. Brom's left wrist wore a linen cuff, and he was to hang nothing from it until the middle of the eighty-seventh day. Karis had been told to ask nothing of herself for three days more, and she was asleep against a box.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-23.md:231:"Tomorrow is the ninetieth," she said. "The plank, and a smith. I have a slip in my coat with a horned head on it, and I want to hear what he does with a job that ended in a no." She turned a leaf. "And Thornwater on the ninety-third. That's four days, and two of them are road."
