editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:549:There were eight more. One wanted a night-watch kept on the landing, and one wanted stones picked out of a field, and one was a message to be walked to a hold four days off, for a mark and feed. Most were in the same square black hand, as if one person had written them out for others; but beside the words on each somebody had drawn a little picture, a wheel or a fence or a boat with sticks standing in it, for the use of people who could make nothing of the words.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:2281:He had no word to give them. A man did not speak to a bottom line that had cost him nothing. If they were what four lines said, then the board would put them across his road before the snow, and there would be something to say then, and something to price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-46.md:59:"He's just told you what it is. It's got a ruled edge and a word for itself. I don't need it read to me a third time. There's a walk on that oak at fifty that nobody's scratched, a string of salt to the middle holds before the pass shuts. There's a fence at forty, the day the hold comes off it. That's ninety marks of work that was posted by people who want a fence. We'd be down from both before the snow."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:501:That was the whole of it. Five words had gone out from a desk by a noon dispatch, after a man had weighed them for four days on a post road and found them worth sending though they would stop nothing. They had stopped nothing. They were in the minute as an absence, between the count of the exhibits and the count of the orders, and the clerk was already reading the next line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:557:"Call days," she said. "Four of them, before any ruling. In those four days a seat may recall a party to put a question it has thought of late, and so may its evaluation seat, and the code gives them an hour's notice to do it in. An hour, on foot, from wherever the party is lodged." She looked out at the switchbacks. "That was a fair rule when every respondent lived over his own shop in the town. It was not written with a bluff in mind. Your hill is an hour and a quarter from that room by a good horse, and so for four days the house must live where it can hear the exchange's bell. The code calls it keeping within the bell. I have always thought it rather a handsome phrase for a nuisance."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:561:"In my time? Twice. Once to ask a guild master his mother's maiden name, which had been left off a form." The counsel's mouth moved at one corner. "Seats do not think of things late. They are very thorough about thinking of them early. But the rule stands, and we keep it, and in four days nobody will be able to say that the house was not where it was told to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:1091:She got in. For a moment, before the door shut, he saw her face with nobody looking at it, and it was the face of a woman who has known a thing for four days and is not going to say it in a stable yard. He did not understand that then, and put it away to look at later.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:1519:"*Resigned in good standing.*" She said it without surprise. "I know the door. I have known it for four days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:1555:"So I kept it," she said. "For four days, through a return and a ruling. I let you hear the hood say *revoked* without knowing how short the time was. I should like to say that it was easy and that I never wavered, and I can't; I sat in a carriage this afternoon and very nearly said it through the window." Her mouth moved a little. "I wanted it to be yours. If you went, I wanted you to go because you had priced it with your own people, at a table, with my need left out of the sum. And if you stayed, I meant to walk beside you into that frame-house and take what they wrote."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:1561:He found that he could not answer. He had been keeping the largest thing he knew from her for half a year, and it had sat between them like a lie in every room; she had kept a thing from him for four days, and he saw now which of the two silences had been the kinder.
