editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial.stdout.log:4198:"So I kept it," she said. "For four days, through a return and a ruling. I let you hear the hood say *revoked* without knowing how short the time was. I should like to say that it was easy and that I never wavered, and I can't; I sat in a carriage this afternoon and very nearly said it through the window." Her mouth moved a little. "I wanted it to be yours. If you went, I wanted you to go because you had priced it with your own people, at a table, with my need left out of the sum. And if you stayed, I meant to walk beside you into that frame-house and take what they wrote."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/review-editorial.stdout.log:4204:He found that he could not answer. He had been keeping the largest thing he knew from her for half a year, and it had sat between them like a lie in every room; she had kept a thing from him for four days, and he saw now which of the two silences had been the kinder.
