editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:1449:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22:| 7 | Corridor | 5,438 | 5 | **Paragraph nine:** Bracken knows *evaluation integrity* from his own filing (an Ostrand frame reading Stones a rank high); the counsel's twelve sections, never before turned on a person; "I'm the frame." / "A frame that will not read true comes off the floor." Remedy, paragraph 34. The counsel: "A count is evidence. Indignation never was." **Chapter fourteen** in Bracken's flattest voice (Tier B); "Somebody… imagined you." **Withrow's morning after**: the ferry pass, the guild hall, the sealed file, the house's letter; **"It's expulsion that follows you."**; the two restrictions and the daughter at her counter every week for a year. **Bracken's pocket calendar:** dated the first day, served the eighth, seven days at a walk ("sent to be watched getting here"), **due the twenty-second**; *respondent made default*. **Karis's six slips**; **"It's not a question. It's a corridor. Every door in it is real law, and every door opens one way."**; "The house will answer"; *fled*; four days. **The stratum note, sideways:** "They're trying to move him back inside the instrument." / "I don't know why that distinction feels important. Noting it." A question mark in Cael's notebook. **The residence awake for her:** Seln's lamp in the wing; Brom's tea kept hot for hours, four cups; Karis counts the room; "Thank you for the tea." Cael tells it; **Brom: "Corridor."**; **Lira: "What if the people didn't fail this time?"**; "Then there's a place where they read it wrong." **The first pole**, verbatim, in one pass; the records hall's lamps out in pairs; the copy on the sill, first page up, **waiting for better light** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:1833:- **What Leaving Costs**: three roads priced; the cache argued for and lost out loud; **Bracken brings Brom's finding at night** — Iron, found, and the guidance note — "How many boxes is your research?" / "Three." / "Then I'm carrying three boxes."; Lira's whole bill; Karis's forfeiture priced in bibliography order (the Greyvane request redirected to Hesk; the assistant's letter); Seln's one sentence; **Ephram brought in, told the departure and nothing of the cache, asks for one bout**; five hands, Seln's last. **Withrow** alone: the four days she knew and said nothing; the other column; **"The record will say you left…"**; she opens the door herself. **Lira's window** (~1.5k) that night.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:1847:The closings' rhetoric inside the given claims; the four days' scenes; the council's order beyond the fixed beats; the bout's sequences inside the four exchanges given; the yard's light; who cries and who doesn't (Bracken already did).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:1912:- **Why four days in Ostrand:** "call days". An old rule of the code: in the four days before a ruling a seat, or its evaluation seat, may recall a party upon an hour's notice, so the parties keep "within the bell" of the seat. The house takes the upper floor of the wool-factors' guesting-house in the lane behind the exchange. Brom is there for his panel in the same town; Lira by Rooke's leave ("She's drilled in worse"). Seln stays on the hill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:1915:- **"Five weeks became five days":** the code's notice for a compelled evaluation is five clear days. The district clerk reserved the frame-house for the first lawful date before the ruling was given (a prudent clerk books a frame). Bracken read the reservation on the district's board on the first call day; the counsel showed Withrow the arithmetic that evening: the notice will be served the morning after the ruling, for a day inside the year, while he is still her enrollee — she must then produce him with her own hand or refuse a seat. The only course that leaves the house clean and him out of the frame is that he withdraw first. She has known four days and has not said so, so that the going would be his and not her need.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:1976:1. **Withrow, alone.** Her lamp; the folder open at the eighth day; the right-hand column still empty. The four days she knew: the reserved frame, the five days' notice, the counsel's advice she would not pass on. "Five weeks became five days." The other column: what the clerk will write. "The record will say you left. I'll spend the rest of my tenure making the record say why." She opens the door herself.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:2142:    59	Between the two sittings there were four days, and the four days were their own kind of instruction.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:2144:    61	The delegation stayed at Ostrand in the guesting-house on the cathedral street, because going back to the bluff and returning would have cost two days of coach. They ate together in the evenings. Karis worked; she had a supplemental submission to draft on a point the seal had raised, and she drafted it, and it was good, and she knew while she was drafting it that the seal had raised the point out of courtesy and would rule the other way. Brom found a yard behind the guesting-house and used it, one-handed at first and then with both, and Lira came down and worked opposite him on the second morning, on an ankle that had come out of its strapping two weeks before, and neither of them said anything about the four days or the ruling or the road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:2301:    43	The knock came at the records hall's door at the ninth bell and it was Bracken, who did not attend councils and would not have entered one, standing in the corridor with his coat still on and an envelope held level in both hands the way he held everything that had come off a counter. A district officer had ridden up the bluff at dusk with it. The advancement review had been docketed for the last Fifth-day of term, four days out — four days after the ruling, a different seat, the registry giving one man his tier in the same week it decided his friend had none and never noticing it had written a joke. But the review's *finding* had come early and hand-delivered, because a finding this clean did not wait for its own hearing, and the district seat had wanted it in the practitioner's hands before the term's other news reached the district seat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:2389:   131	"I checked it four times the night the ruling landed," she said. "It is my office to know the respondent's best remaining move before the respondent does. It is not my office to recommend it, because a chancellor who recommends resignation to an enrollee under proceedings has done the petitioner's work for him at no charge, and I would have had to enter that in my own ledger, and I keep that ledger the way Bracken keeps his." She squared the copy to the desk's edge. "So I have known the answer for four days and said nothing, and waited to see whether you would arrive at it, and you have arrived at it, and I am now permitted to tell you that it is correct. That is the whole of what the office allows me, and I want you to understand that I have used every inch of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:2403:   145	He believed her, and entered the believing rather than the sentence, because the sentence was the kind a person says at a door and the believing was the part that would still be true in ten years. She did not offer her hand and he did not expect it. She walked him to the office door and opened it herself, which she did for visiting officers of grade and had never once done for an enrollee, and Cael, going down the stair, understood that he had just been promoted out of the institution by its chancellor four days before he resigned from it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:3003:   213	That was the whole of it. Five words had gone out from a desk by a noon dispatch, after a man had weighed them for four days on a post road and found them worth sending though they would stop nothing. They had stopped nothing. They were in the minute as an absence, between the count of the exhibits and the count of the orders, and the clerk was already reading the next line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:3058:     5	"Call days," she said. "Four of them, before any ruling. In those four days a seat may recall a party to put a question it has thought of late, and so may its evaluation seat, and the code gives them an hour's notice to do it in. An hour, on foot, from wherever the party is lodged." She looked out at the switchbacks. "That was a fair rule when every respondent lived over his own shop in the town. It was not written with a bluff in mind. Your hill is an hour and a quarter from that room by a good horse, and so for four days the house must live where it can hear the exchange's bell. The code calls it keeping within the bell. I have always thought it rather a handsome phrase for a nuisance."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:3062:     9	"In my time? Twice. Once to ask a guild master his mother's maiden name, which had been left off a form." The counsel's mouth moved at one corner. "Seats do not think of things late. They are very thorough about thinking of them early. But the rule stands, and we keep it, and in four days nobody will be able to say that the house was not where it was told to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:3591:   239	She got in. For a moment, before the door shut, he saw her face with nobody looking at it, and it was the face of a woman who has known a thing for four days and is not going to say it in a stable yard. He did not understand that then, and put it away to look at later.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:4278:    17	"*Resigned in good standing.*" She said it without surprise. "I know the door. I have known it for four days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:4314:    53	"So I kept it," she said. "For four days, through a return and a ruling. I let you hear the hood say *revoked* without knowing how short the time was. I should like to say that it was easy and that I never wavered, and I can't; I sat in a carriage this afternoon and very nearly said it through the window." Her mouth moved a little. "I wanted it to be yours. If you went, I wanted you to go because you had priced it with your own people, at a table, with my need left out of the sum. And if you stayed, I meant to walk beside you into that frame-house and take what they wrote."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:4320:    59	He found that he could not answer. He had been keeping the largest thing he knew from her for half a year, and it had sat between them like a lie in every room; she had kept a thing from him for four days, and he saw now which of the two silences had been the kinder.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/source-tracking.stdout.log:5315:    syllable of it"; **the declined certification entered as an absence**; four days in Ostrand
