editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:291:There was one thing more, and she had kept it for the last of the oil. She had been over the Fallow's eleven strips for four days at a trestle in a barn, and she had every stroke of them by heart.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:295:"This one. It's not on the Ring. I looked for it for four days and it isn't on any upright. It's here, on every wall, and it's not in the courses with the rest — it's *between* them. On its own. Here." The pencil moved along the sheet to the next one, and the next. "And here. And here. I've paced the spacing because I pace things. It comes every — " she looked at the notebook, where she had written it, and read it out as a number she had checked twice — "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride. It recurs, on the wall, at the perimeter's radius."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-24.md:51:"Who they ought to have. One's a bull wants bringing down off the top grazing before the snow shuts it, and he's killed a dog. The other's a ford that wants staking. They'd each of them heard a line said in this meadow about a river and five dead hounds." He blotted something. "I told them you were six days off on a hill. They said they'd wait a fortnight. After that they'll have Teague."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.md:60:**Governing text.** The ratified calendar says: “ruling and Brom's panel DAY 201; … academic year closes DAY 207; the Registry Line is crossed after day 207” (`STATE_LEDGER.md:992–1025`). The provisional clean door is withdrawal “after a ruling and before a revocation's effect,” entered as *resigned in good standing* (`STATE_LEDGER.md:954,980`; B6 `BOOK_MAP.md:437–443`). M9 enters day 203, “four days before the academic year's close” (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:13–15`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.md:108:**Page.** The counsel explains four call days and the requirement to remain within an hour of the bell (`manuscript/chapter-50.md:3–23`). The four days then develop Brom/Lira, Karis's supplemental, the district-station girl, Ilsev, and Havel (`manuscript/chapter-50.md:49–295`; `manuscript/chapter-51.md:3–123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/plan-audit.md:110:**Governing text.** The packet requires “Four days in Ostrand” and assigns those exact episodes to them (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23–24`); `BOOK_MAP.md` likewise requires “The four days in Ostrand before the ruling” (`BOOK_MAP.md:384–394`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-54.md:41:He did the other thing, which he had done in a room under a floor four days before without being asked. He stepped up beside her, and turned his left side to the wall, and bent his back, with his one good hand on his knee.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-40.md:285:"It's been off the tree longer than any apple on that shelf. That brown you're so fond of came down a fortnight after it, and it'll be meal before the snow's a week old." He had turned, and was reaching up to a shelf over the hearth, into the dark behind a row of crocks; and what he brought down was green, and long, and wrinkled like an old woman's knuckle. "That's the same tree as your sour one, and it's last year's. Go on."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-35.md:163:So she walked like a duck, across a country with nothing in it but grass, at the pace of a small brown animal that never hurried and never stopped. She had hated that pace for four days on a mountain. She found now that she could not have gone faster if she had been let, and it was restful, in its way, to have the matter settled by somebody else's legs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-35.md:215:*Later.* It was still on her side. She could wait. She had waited four days on a mountain to admit that a mule had a kind eye.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-35.md:341:"Tomorrow. First light. The back room, with the door shut, and I'll not have eaten, so nor will you. It's both hands. It's twenty minutes, near enough; I'll not know till I'm in." She tucked the stick into her coat. "It costs me a mending, and there's a bench under that window I owe four days to. They'll keep till after noon. I've looked at every one of them."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-42.md:117:"There's a child. You told us about a child with a chest. I can keep it still for four days; I've kept it still for ten."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-45.md:47:He could do the second tonight. Four people were asleep or near it, and the fire was low. He had his fingers on his own wrist before he saw what he was about.
