editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:5903:    21	He got the trouser leg up and the binding off. The ford's line along the inside of the calf, opened on the rim's edge four days ago and washed and bound at the stone and not touched since, was a seam. Pink, closed its whole length, the black gone out of it. She put a thumb along it and pressed, and he did not move, and she pressed harder, and he did not move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:6703:    21	He got the trouser leg up and the binding off. The ford's line along the inside of the calf, opened on the rim's edge four days ago and washed and bound at the stone and not touched since, was a seam. Pink, closed its whole length, the black gone out of it. She put a thumb along it and pressed, and he did not move, and she pressed harder, and he did not move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:8410:   163	So she walked like a duck, across a country with nothing in it but grass, at the pace of a small brown animal that never hurried and never stopped. She had hated that pace for four days on a mountain. She found now that she could not have gone faster if she had been let, and it was restful, in its way, to have the matter settled by somebody else's legs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:8462:   215	*Later.* It was still on her side. She could wait. She had waited four days on a mountain to admit that a mule had a kind eye.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:8586:   339	"Tomorrow. First light. The back room, with the door shut, and I'll not have eaten, so nor will you. It's both hands. It's twenty minutes, near enough; I'll not know till I'm in." She tucked the stick into her coat. "It costs me a mending, and there's a bench under that window I owe four days to. They'll keep till after noon. I've looked at every one of them."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:9063:    51	"Who they ought to have. One's a bull wants bringing down off the top grazing before the snow shuts it, and he's killed a dog. The other's a ford that wants staking. They'd each of them heard a line said in this meadow about a river and five dead hounds." He blotted something. "I told them you were six days off on a hill. They said they'd wait a fortnight. After that they'll have Teague."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:9374:    81	The price came first, and it was a hundred, which was too much. A surveyor's kit was a thing that one man carried on a strap; he had seen such a kit once, years ago and a long way west. It was two days out to that rise and two home, on a road he knew, and nobody paid a hundred marks for four days and a case. But *too much* was only a reason if a man could say what it was too much for, and he could not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:9442:   149	All of those were his, and he saw that each of them was a way of dressing the plain thing so that it should look better on him. The plain thing was that five people had a hundred and eight marks and the cold coming, and that this paid as much again for four days of road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:9538:   245	"So we could go four days and come home with a line and no money."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:9605:    51	"Who they ought to have. One's a bull wants bringing down off the top grazing before the snow shuts it, and he's killed a dog. The other's a ford that wants staking. They'd each of them heard a line said in this meadow about a river and five dead hounds." He blotted something. "I told them you were six days off on a hill. They said they'd wait a fortnight. After that they'll have Teague."
