editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:17587:   431	**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the ten audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (three more lines in Teague's window changed so he cannot tie the healer's lateness to the five); six tracked passages restaged; about 1,480 words of repeated survey procedure removed; orienting sentences at the split; the day-80 log reads "Some of the herd went over the edge after the cart. How many: heard, not sworn…"; a day-84 reset at Teague's window; Oryn's sum reconciled (whole on the 99th; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; a plan of four days at Thornwater's table plus one added day, which she changes at Thornwater's gate on the 93rd). New: Seln reads a heavy clawless footmark at a seep (unidentified sign; KEEP). Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — one applied (ch16: Seln shows the width with his hands). All six tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 28 protected. 41439 words. Coordinator correction logged: the Bodies bullet first mis-stated whose leg was mended; corrected above and the Movement 4 author told.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:17613:   457	- **The two HOLD slips (flag):** one bark and one shingle; a bull to be brought down off top grazing before the snow, and a ford to be staked. Each hold "asked who". They will wait a fortnight for the five and then have Teague. Cael tells Pike on the 91st not to keep them past the fortnight. **They are still on the oak at the end of the movement.**
