editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/plan-audit.stdout.log:19411:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-35.md:339:"Tomorrow. First light. The back room, with the door shut, and I'll not have eaten, so nor will you. It's both hands. It's twenty minutes, near enough; I'll not know till I'm in." She tucked the stick into her coat. "It costs me a mending, and there's a bench under that window I owe four days to. They'll keep till after noon. I've looked at every one of them."
