editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2605:- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2647:| 18 | Tape; the lip; four days down; the route told (seven holds, twenty days); "The route is the only thing I own."; Oxhollow's table; the map paid; three readings; the two readings taught; three questions; "Thornwater's on my route in nine days…"; Teague at the ford: "The bench was a cart." (Ch7) | 81–84 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2677:2. **The compressed roads and recoveries put on the page (+38,000).** The source summarizes the six days in the fin's lee and on the mountain's lip (+4k); the four days down to Oxhollow (+4k); the six days Oxhollow→Lowmarch (+4k); days 60–69 at Lowmarch and the well on the south road (+8k); the two days stone→Thornwater with Lira flat-footed (+3k); Thornwater→Lowmarch in the first cold (+2k); the three-day bearing walk (+4k); and the six days from the fourth site home in first snow (+5k). Thornwater's three stays get texture as a place that becomes home (+4k). *Why:* the arc's freedom is made of walking and of places that feed them, and the source keeps cutting it to a sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2713:**Two hard rules for every window:** (1) **No member of Teague's crew is named, ever**, including in Teague's own head. Book 8 kills "the young one" at the pass and says his name once without entering it. Teague thinks of his people as the spear, the bow, the boy and the healer, which is how a captain counts. (2) **Oryn's holds stay unnamed** except Oxhollow, Thornwater and Millrace. In her head they are what they owe her or what is there: the hold with the child; the hold that gave the coat; the fourth, four days on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2893:- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2909:| The still place | Located (M6, unnamed); named as *the still place* (M8); read three times; "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment." | *source, before, primordial, recurrence* (Book 9's word); a Rune-like "shape with bones" (Book 8's); any theory, including Oryn's |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:3015:- **Road times (prose, fixed):** Lowmarch ↔ Thornwater two days; Thornwater → the Fallow rise two days; Lowmarch → Oxhollow six days (north-west); Lowmarch → Millrace one day south on the Stair road; Millrace's fork → the Stair's line the same afternoon; the Stair → the Hall three days along the bearing; the Hall → the fork one day; the fork → the fourth site a day and a half; the fourth site → Lowmarch six days; the fourth site's gap → Thornwater four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:3355:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:3391:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the ten audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (three more lines in Teague's window changed so he cannot tie the healer's lateness to the five); six tracked passages restaged; about 1,480 words of repeated survey procedure removed; orienting sentences at the split; the day-80 log reads "Some of the herd went over the edge after the cart. How many: heard, not sworn…"; a day-84 reset at Teague's window; Oryn's sum reconciled (whole on the 99th; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; a plan of four days at Thornwater's table plus one added day, which she changes at Thornwater's gate on the 93rd). New: Seln reads a heavy clawless footmark at a seep (unidentified sign; KEEP). Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — one applied (ch16: Seln shows the width with his hands). All six tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 28 protected. 41439 words. Coordinator correction logged: the Bodies bullet first mis-stated whose leg was mended; corrected above and the Movement 4 author told.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:3417:- **The two HOLD slips (flag):** one bark and one shingle; a bull to be brought down off top grazing before the snow, and a ford to be staked. Each hold "asked who". They will wait a fortnight for the five and then have Teague. Cael tells Pike on the 91st not to keep them past the fortnight. **They are still on the oak at the end of the movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:3441:**Calendar.** Sunset on the **ninety-sixth day past the Line**, at the eastern lip of the Fallow Ring's floor. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term"; "frost"; "before the snow"; "fortnight"). Days on the page: 84 (dusk), 85, 86, 87, 88, 89, 90, 91, 92, 93, 94, 95, 96; and, in Teague's window, the evening of the 89th. Weather: frost every morning; dry roads; a north wind on the Fallow. The next movement opens where this one stops.
