came at the records hall's door at the ninth bell and it was Bracken, who did not attend councils and would not have entered one, standing in the corridor with his coat still on and an envelope held level in both hands the way he held everything that had come off a counter. A district officer had ridden up the bluff at dusk with it. The advancement review had been docketed for the last Fifth-day of term, four days out — four days after the ruling, a different seat, the registry giving one man his tier in the same week it decided his friend had none and never noticing it had written a joke. But the review's *finding* had come early and hand-delivered, because a finding this clean did not wait for its own hearing, and the district seat had wanted it in the practitioner's hands before the term's other news reached the district seat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:2753:   131	"I checked it four times the night the ruling landed," she said. "It is my office to know the respondent's best remaining move before the respondent does. It is not my office to recommend it, because a chancellor who recommends resignation to an enrollee under proceedings has done the petitioner's work for him at no charge, and I would have had to enter that in my own ledger, and I keep that ledger the way Bracken keeps his." She squared the copy to the desk's edge. "So I have known the answer for four days and said nothing, and waited to see whether you would arrive at it, and you have arrived at it, and I am now permitted to tell you that it is correct. That is the whole of what the office allows me, and I want you to understand that I have used every inch of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:2767:   145	He believed her, and entered the believing rather than the sentence, because the sentence was the kind a person says at a door and the believing was the part that would still be true in ten years. She did not offer her hand and he did not expect it. She walked him to the office door and opened it herself, which she did for visiting officers of grade and had never once done for an enrollee, and Cael, going down the stair, understood that he had just been promoted out of the institution by its chancellor four days before he resigned from it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:3002:    71	He noted, without particular interest, that he had no plan for the rest of his life beyond the next four days. He had never had one. Fifteen years of a trade in which the future is somebody else's product had left him with a mind that saw one week clearly and nothing after it, and he expected he would find that inconvenient eventually, and expected also that the researcher would have opinions about it, and expected further that the opinions would be correct and that he would take them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:3046:   115	Afterward the talk went where talk goes on a first night out, which is everywhere except the thing. Lira ran the road east and wanted to know what the last four days looked like and got, from Seln, an answer of such precision that Karis stopped writing and started listening: the ford at the second day and its condition after rain; the chartered waystation on the third and the fact that its posting-board was current, which meant a rider still came out to it; the provincial marker and what would be standing at it; and the river crossing on the fourth with the last station on the far bank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:3074:   143	*Four files closed complete at a counter, and one man who filed nothing, and squared his keys, and walked east in the dark, and stopped once to look back and didn't know how. The office found the empty desk this morning and started, a day late, to wonder what he kept. Let them wonder. It's four days east of anywhere they can execute a wondering, and the case is under the same canvas as Karis's boxes, and tomorrow we cross the last thing the registry drew on a map.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:3524:   183	There was no moon, and the cloud had not lifted in four days. Past the stable passage the dark came down like a sack, and Cael stood in it at the top of the farm track with the others breathing round him and could not see his own hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:3649:     9	Lira was at her chalk at the south end with her back to the door. She had taped her own wrists but not the ankle, because the healer had said there was nothing left in it to tape, and she stood now with her weight even on both feet and her left arm tucked a little toward her ribs, from the old habit, and did not look round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:3803:   163	She had started it in the dairy week. Not that night; the night after, when she could not sleep for thinking about three carters and a road with four days of stamps on it and then none. She had thought then, lying on her back in the dark, about what she actually owned. Not the program. The program was Rooke's, and the east hall was the house's, and the red book belonged to a river academy and was only lent. The figure on the steward's sheet was hers, but it was hers the way a room is yours when somebody else holds the key; it meant something because a hall's seal was on it, and it would go on meaning something exactly as far as that seal was honoured.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:3962:    75	He looked for it, quite honestly. They had spent four days on that table of renewals, in the annex, at the start of the year. He had found the nine days himself, in his own old Log, and Karis had let him find them. He had been proud of it for a week. And a man in a mended coat had just stood up before a hood and said that every line of it was right, and adopted it, and thrown away a piece of his own petition rather than leave an error standing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:4776:   283	He knew what would be done with it. The code let a seat proceed upon its own authority where a certificate was withheld; he had cited that section himself, once, long ago, when a guild hall's assessor would not sign. His line would stop nothing. The sittings would sit, and the ruling would be read, and somewhere in a minute a clerk would enter that a thing usually present was not there. That was the whole of what he could do, and he had weighed it on a post road for four days and found that it was still worth doing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:5709:books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-14.md:5:The note came up from the assessment office at the seventh bell, on the counter's ordinary stock, in the counter's ordinary hand, addressed to the delegation's floor coordinator and copied nowhere: *Wing three practice allocation revised. Enrollee's supervised hours suspended four days pending recovery-of-form. Reallocation to follow.* It was a true document about a true thing and it said nothing whatever, and Cael read it lying flat on his back on the residence floor with his boots still on, because the floor was the only surface in the room that had stopped moving, and thought, with the part of him that was still able to draft sentences, that the man had built a postponement out of a scheduling instrument in under an hour and had probably not thought of it as difficult.
