editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.stdout.log:4035:   133	The grey rider had come up closer than he had been in four days, perhaps eighty yards off. He was mounted again, and he rode up the last of the rise at a walk, and stopped at the pillar's foot on its western side, with the cob's nose level with the stone. He did not come past it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.stdout.log:4043:   141	He looked at each of them in turn, as the elder coat had done at the road's foot, and at Seln a little longer than the rest, and his face did not change. It was a plain weathered face. He had stood by a milestone with a tin cup through a recess and eleven sittings, and he had ridden four days at their backs without once pretending to be anything else.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.stdout.log:4437:    41	He did not ask anybody. He went round the foot of the block, where the pine had been dropping dead limbs for longer than there had been a road, and gathered them up, and broke them across his knee and laid them small to large. He was quicker at it than he had been four days ago, and he had the fire's place chosen, in the lee of the stone, before the gelding was out of the shafts.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.stdout.log:5173:    41	He did not ask anybody. He went round the foot of the block, where the pine had been dropping dead limbs for longer than there had been a road, and gathered them up, and broke them across his knee and laid them small to large. He was quicker at it than he had been four days ago, and he had the fire's place chosen, in the lee of the stone, before the gelding was out of the shafts.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.stdout.log:5554:    22	- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.stdout.log:6212:   113	There were eight more. One wanted a night-watch kept on the landing, and one wanted stones picked out of a field, and one was a message to be walked to a hold four days off, for a mark and feed. Most were in the same square black hand, as if one person had written them out for others; but beside the words on each somebody had drawn a little picture, a wheel or a fence or a boat with sticks standing in it, for the use of people who could make nothing of the words.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.stdout.log:7926:   355	He had no word to give them, for a man did not speak to a bottom line that had cost him nothing. If they were what four lines said, then the board would put them across his road before the snow, and there would be something to say then, and something to price.
