editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:4488:   109	The healer did not answer at once. He saw her look at his right hand, where it hung, and then at her own wrist; and for the space of one breath there was the hunger in her face that he had seen at a ford and in a yard, when she had wanted to know a thing more than she wanted her supper. She put it by as he had seen her put it by before.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:4506:   127	"She looked at your hand before she said it," Karis murmured. Her voice was pitched for his ear alone. "And then at her own wrist. I have seen that look on a person in front of a shut press. She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere."
