editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:5072:   167	One by one they came down and tried it, since no one of them would take another's word for such a thing: Lira, and Brom, and Seln, each a stride past the stone and a stride back. The healer went over last, with two fingers on her own wrist and her lips moving, and came out again and nodded. Cael walked across beside Brom, and felt what he had felt on the Fallow, which was grass under his boots.
