editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:8618:   291	There was one thing more, and she had kept it for the last of the oil. She had been over the Fallow's eleven strips for four days at a trestle in a barn, and she had every stroke of them by heart.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:8622:   295	"This one. It's not on the Ring. I looked for it for four days and it isn't on any upright. It's here, on every wall, and it's not in the courses with the rest — it's *between* them. On its own. Here." The pencil moved along the sheet to the next one, and the next. "And here. And here. I've paced the spacing because I pace things. It comes every — " she looked at the notebook, where she had written it, and read it out as a number she had checked twice — "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride. It recurs, on the wall, at the perimeter's radius."
