editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:20050:   109	Then she let herself go over the other, since she had four days and nobody to see her do it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:20070:   129	The gap took the four days that a carter's skin had given it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:20092:   151	She was a very small old woman. Oryn had mended that knee at a mill, thirteen days before, and had seen its owner go away up a valley on a hurdle between two grandsons. She came over the low place every year before the snow, to her daughter's hearth in this long house; and Oryn had told her, as the hurdle was lifted, that she would see the knee here, after the thaw.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:20102:   161	Oryn got down on her heels in the frost, and put both hands round the joint. Her lips went to three. It was all there: the old banks, worn as smooth as a doorstep, and the current going through the place where a ladder had been as though no ladder had ever stood in it. She had promised that knee a look after the thaw, and it had walked over a hill to be looked at before the snow.
