editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27258:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:31:- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27271:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:73:| 18 | Tape; the lip; four days down; the route told (seven holds, twenty days); "The route is the only thing I own."; Oxhollow's table; the map paid; three readings; the two readings taught; three questions; "Thornwater's on my route in nine days…"; Teague at the ford: "The bench was a cart." (Ch7) | 81–84 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27282:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:103:2. **The compressed roads and recoveries put on the page (+38,000).** The source summarizes the six days in the fin's lee and on the mountain's lip (+4k); the four days down to Oxhollow (+4k); the six days Oxhollow→Lowmarch (+4k); days 60–69 at Lowmarch and the well on the south road (+8k); the two days stone→Thornwater with Lira flat-footed (+3k); Thornwater→Lowmarch in the first cold (+2k); the three-day bearing walk (+4k); and the six days from the fourth site home in first snow (+5k). Thornwater's three stays get texture as a place that becomes home (+4k). *Why:* the arc's freedom is made of walking and of places that feed them, and the source keeps cutting it to a sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27290:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:139:**Two hard rules for every window:** (1) **No member of Teague's crew is named, ever**, including in Teague's own head. Book 8 kills "the young one" at the pass and says his name once without entering it. Teague thinks of his people as the spear, the bow, the boy and the healer, which is how a captain counts. (2) **Oryn's holds stay unnamed** except Oxhollow, Thornwater and Millrace. In her head they are what they owe her or what is there: the hold with the child; the hold that gave the coat; the fourth, four days on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27341:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:319:- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27367:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:49:Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27393:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/STATE_LEDGER.md:54:- **Road times (prose, fixed):** Lowmarch ↔ Thornwater two days; Thornwater → the Fallow rise two days; Lowmarch → Oxhollow six days (north-west); Lowmarch → Millrace one day south on the Stair road; Millrace's fork → the Stair's line the same afternoon; the Stair → the Hall three days along the bearing; the Hall → the fork one day; the fork → the fourth site a day and a half; the fourth site → Lowmarch six days; the fourth site's gap → Thornwater four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27438:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈29,900. **Teague cutaway ≈1,700** (days 117–120: following the crew's trail three days along a bearing he does not understand, the healer brought because a shoulder was mended once; sitting down beside the boy; the column). **Karis cutaway ≈2,000** (days 119–120 at the far fire: three copies, the ledger, the edge laid and moved; it ends exactly on the pencil stopping; no who or why). **Seln cutaway ≈1,600** (days 124–128, the road home: the ledger in his coat; giving it to Karis and not asking for it back). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,800** (day 122 to about 128: the gap north-west, four days, three weeks late; Thornwater; the old woman's knee; writing the letter, ending on its four lines).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27443:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof-part4.stdout.log:27472:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:25:- **Two days back (98–99):** Lira walking flat-footed as she is told; the calf closing with no count on the flat by the second noon. **Thornwater:** "Six. Well." Tape off in the yard ("Twenty-one days. A rib is six weeks. These are done."). The calf closed in four days. "Still and whole." / "You don't get a yes. You get told." / "What does helping look like?" / "I'll know."
