editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:633:Lira was at her chalk at the south end with her back to the door. She had taped her own wrists but not the ankle, because the healer had said there was nothing left in it to tape, and she stood now with her weight even on both feet and her left arm tucked a little toward her ribs, from the old habit, and did not look round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:787:She had started it in the dairy week. Not that night; the night after, when she could not sleep for thinking about three carters and a road with four days of stamps on it and then none. She had thought then, lying on her back in the dark, about what she actually owned. Not the program. The program was Rooke's, and the east hall was the house's, and the red book belonged to a river academy and was only lent. The figure on the steward's sheet was hers, but it was hers the way a room is yours when somebody else holds the key; it meant something because a hall's seal was on it, and it would go on meaning something exactly as far as that seal was honoured.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:947:He looked for it, quite honestly. They had spent four days on that table of renewals, in the annex, at the start of the year. He had found the nine days himself, in his own old Log, and Karis had let him find them. He had been proud of it for a week. And a man in a mended coat had just stood up before a hood and said that every line of it was right, and adopted it, and thrown away a piece of his own petition rather than leave an error standing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:1763:He knew what would be done with it. The code let a seat proceed upon its own authority where a certificate was withheld; he had cited that section himself, once, long ago, when a guild hall's assessor would not sign. His line would stop nothing. The sittings would sit, and the ruling would be read, and somewhere in a minute a clerk would enter that a thing usually present was not there. That was the whole of what he could do, and he had weighed it on a post road for four days and found that it was still worth doing.
