editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:3339:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names. The interval log is day 0. Day 1 is First-day (dawn run and convocation; the instrument is dated this day). Day 2: the Silver floor and the reading room. Day 3: the counter and the north wall. Day 4: the docket at supper. Day 5, Fifth-day: wing three. Day 6, Sixth-day night: the honest floor. Day 7, Seventh-day: rest and Bracken's window. **Day 8, First-day: served**; the procedure runs that night into the small hours of day 9. **The answer is due at the seat in Ostrand by close of business on the twenty-second day.** Karis says the answer's shape will take four days. Brom's sitting is the last Fifth-day of the academic year.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:3536:| 42–57 | ch7 | Redrafted whole. Changes, in order: <ul><li>The counsel: "I've looked tonight for the case where somebody turned these sections round to point at the man standing in the frame… This is new."</li><li>"Do you know the difference, in front of a seat, between a description and an evaluation?"</li><li>Bracken reads "flat"; the clerks' first-year joke ("the only page in the code nobody has ever had to stamp"); "imagined you" kept.</li><li>Withrow's morning after is rebuilt around the ferry, the guild master and the sealed file ("Kept, every page, perfectly safe, and nobody may open it"); "You can walk out of a town. You can't walk out of the post."; "Twice in my registry years I put my name to one. The first I'd sign again tomorrow… The second had a daughter."</li><li>The calendar: three silent marks read out by Karis ("The first. The eighth. The twenty-second."), with "in thirteen years I have never seen a seat take those three words back for anybody's lame horse".</li><li>The six slips are spoken as their words only, with one comment at the fifth.</li><li>The not-a-trick paragraph is now "Bracken would carry a paper like this. So would I… Look for the trick all night and you'll come up empty."</li><li>"the other choice has its own word in the docket, and the word is *fled*… I'll have bones on it in four days."</li><li>The stratum lead-in: "That clause is why you've never stood in a station since Denvash."</li><li>The note goes inside the front cover; the question mark: "She would answer it in her own time."</li><li>Seln's lamp: Cael "did not let himself guess what the man at the copying table was making".</li><li>Karis's instructions are cut to "Four days" and "Thank you for the tea".</li><li>The telling covers what moved the table, in a new order. Brom: "Then what's the answer for?" Cael's answer names the warden, provost and tournament himself; Lira: "And this time?… What if the people didn't fail this time?"; Lira leaves without the "Bed" line; Brom's second "Corridor." comes at the door.</li><li>Pole frame: "The entry was finished before the pen touched paper."</li><li>The prolepsis is trimmed to "It looked like the truth, because, as far as he could see from that window, it was."</li><li>The lamps go out by the hall's own count (the counter pair, the table's pairs from the far end, the press lamp last).</li></ul> |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:3644:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names. Day 9 Second-day: drafting begins (four days to bones). Day 12 Fifth-day: bones. Day 13 night: the integrity section. Day 16: the counter. Two nights of Bracken's reading; the first rain; the weighing. **Day 19, Fifth-day: the answer goes down, three days inside the time** (due day 22). **Day 23: the seat's notice. Day 25, Fourth-day: Jent's conference; Withrow's office that evening.** Day 26 Fifth-day: board line; wing three. Day 27: the coats placed; the honest floor. **Day 30, Second-day: Lira's trial.** Day 31: the district docket's confirmation and the Velmere letter; opened the third evening (day 33). Day 35: Karis's budget; the frames days 35–38. Day 39: the annex convening. **Day 40, Fifth-day (the year's sixth): the first sitting.** **Day 42, Seventh-day: the month's close.** Lira's first meet off the hill is about four weeks away (Rooke's board). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:3825:- (e) The Seln circuit is walked on days 48 (post sort) and 49 (lodge), and the four queries, Hesk's letter, the inventory and Withrow's story all fall on day 49, so the inventory is named inside its sixth week. The source's "four days" between the queries and Hesk's letter became two hours.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:3884:- **The circle:** the road east as Lira's sum (the last Arbiter station four days past Ostrand loaded, three light; stamps stop there; two carters go past, the third turns at it and won't say why); the coastal default and *fled*; forty days after the fourth sitting's close; the five offices' inventories closed (Seln); Jent's sentence on the record; the fossil provision's two paragraphs (the second kept unmentioned); the escort order whole; a "facilities office" nobody can place; **Anchor Path** as a name and a use (rare; service; enforcement; holds people) — **inferred only: no range, rate or cost**; the three-way distinction (Ternhall's anchors / the Lattice Path / Anchor Path).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:4097:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards; Halcenvane weekdays. **Day 88 Fourth-day:** Lira's strapping off (morning); the case opened in the reading room after supper (five arrivals a quarter apart, Cael fourth, Seln on the eighth bell); the mechanism told to Seln; the seal's grounds revised. **Day 89 Fifth-day:** the counter; Brom's sling off at noon; Lira's question on the north wall at dusk. **Day 90 Sixth-day:** Rooke's "Not yet." **Day 91 Seventh-day:** the Greyvane leaves (Bracken, noon); the enrollment book lent; the clean door found that night. **Day 92 First-day:** the enrollment book returned before the second bell; the honest floor, perception only, after the tenth bell. **Day 93 Second-day:** the four findings. **Day 94 Third-day:** Vastin proposed; five hands. **Day 95 Fourth-day:** Seln reads the closures. **Day 96 Fifth-day:** the note left at the inn on the wharf. **Day 98 Seventh-day:** the borrowed office, the second bell after noon; Vastin eleven minutes early (the Ostrand station's inspection that morning). **About day 103:** Vastin at his desk (the "fifth morning after", having walked six river stations in four days). The *fled* default would enter on day 115 if Cael left. The midyear recess is ahead; not dated. Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:4166:- **Vastin (flag):** the river inspection (six stations in four days; one frame shimmed and so certified); the fourth station's keeper and his drawer of sheets with margins; his lens on a cord; he will decline to certify.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-28.md:135:He had laid two things side by side at a wash four days ago, and had refused to rule a line between them for want of a third. A query had come down to a registry from somewhere above it, asking which way certain people had gone. A paper had come over a river with a hundred marks, in the hand of somebody who had learned to write at a ruled desk. And here, on the edge of a place where a carter would not put a wheel, was a bar of iron with a registry's stamp on its neck.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-22.md:65:He lay still on the scrubbed wood and looked at the underside of a turf roof. Nine things lay in him as quiet as he had ever known them; he had held them for eighty-four days, and it had become very like breathing. He could not tell what her fingers were reaching for. He knew only that none of the nine had stirred, and that if one had, he would have felt her feel it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-22.md:213:So he would be whole four days after she had gone. She would be two gates on by then, and the round would not bring her back to Thornwater for twenty days more; and a crew off a board does not keep whole for twenty days. He would be on some other road, and as like as not broken in some other place.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-30.md:131:"Then it stays shut," said Brom. "We've walked four days for a line."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.md:44:The binding shape is explicit in `BOOK_MAP.md:112`: “the ruling in the year's last month; the Line crossed after the year's close.” The last-month row says “Closing sittings; Ilsev; the ruling; the council; the last bout” (`BOOK_MAP.md:122`), followed by “Four days before the year's close → after the close” (`BOOK_MAP.md:123`). M8 enters in “The academic year's last month. Two closing sittings at Ostrand. Brom's review on the year's last Fifth-day” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:13`). M9 enters “The morning after the last bout, four days before the academic year's close” (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:13`) and must end after the Line (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-47.md:109:The healer did not answer at once. He saw her look at his right hand, where it hung, and then at her own wrist; and for the space of one breath there was the hunger in her face that he had seen at a ford and in a yard, when she had wanted to know a thing more than she wanted her supper. She put it by as he had seen her put it by before.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-47.md:127:"She looked at your hand before she said it," Karis murmured. Her voice was pitched for his ear alone. "And then at her own wrist. I have seen that look on a person in front of a shut press. She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-60.md:109:Then she let herself go over the other, since she had four days and nobody to see her do it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-60.md:129:The gap took the four days that a carter's skin had given it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-60.md:151:She was a very small old woman. Oryn had mended that knee at a mill, thirteen days before, and had seen its owner go away up a valley on a hurdle between two grandsons. She came over the low place every year before the snow, to her daughter's hearth in this long house; and Oryn had told her, as the hurdle was lifted, that she would see the knee here, after the thaw.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-60.md:161:Oryn got down on her heels in the frost, and put both hands round the joint. Her lips went to three. It was all there: the old banks, worn as smooth as a doorstep, and the current going through the place where a ladder had been as though no ladder had ever stood in it. She had promised that knee a look after the thaw, and it had walked over a hill to be looked at before the snow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.md:41:Oryn's sum now states every needed term: the ribs break on day 78; twenty-one days makes Cael whole on day 99 by her rule; the deep reading can first run on day 100; her ordinary Thornwater stop would end on day 95; four intervening days can be honest table work; the reading day cannot, so `She put a day on the route.` The plan is consistent with the later packets **because it is her day-92 intention and is visibly changed at Thornwater's gate on day 93**. Movement 4 has her say `You're a stop. I've added you`, walk the Fallow road on days 94–95, and remain with the six through the Ring; Movement 5 returns them to Thornwater on day 99 and runs the deep reading on day 100. The BOOK_MAP table fixes those same days. Do **not** take the author's offered cut: removing the second half of `She took it out of the round` would erase the clean distinction between four days she initially counts as route work and the one day she knowingly adds, without improving downstream continuity.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-29.md:65:They waited, and the big brown wrists stayed the colour of wrists. He turned them over to look at the insides, and turned them back.
