editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:4867:    19	The walk-out in its exact images, and its discipline is smallness. Then the empty desk, the machine's paperwork closing on air, four days of road on which the apparatus thins to nothing, the unmarked Line, and the first fire no Arbiter has measured. A deliberately quiet movement: its physical challenge is distance — the ford, the ridge with a blowing horse, scree switchbacks, a camp made from nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:5014:editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:29:- **Day 81 onward:** tape, explained ("It tells the ribs where the edge is"); the lip, thirty-one paces; **four days down** with her walk catalogued (carter's pace; the down-slope side of the mule; the raw heel taped, because she can't heal herself). **Field care taught** (Lira learns to tape her own ankle properly; Brom learns what a wrapped wrist allows). **The ankle refused** on the arithmetic: "That's a tape and a season." **The route told** at the second night's fire: seven, twenty days, thirty-odd rounds, late eleven times and now twelve, what each owes and what she owes; "That's what late is. It's not a number. It's who I don't know about."; "I remember who I've had my hands on… That's the book."; the city's list by tier; the want (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:5465:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-44.md:75:He looked for it, quite honestly. They had spent four days on that table of renewals, in the annex, at the start of the year. He had found the nine days himself, in his own old Log, and Karis had let him find them. He had been proud of it for a week. And a man in a mended coat had just stood up before a hood and said that every line of it was right, and adopted it, and thrown away a piece of his own petition rather than leave an error standing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6280:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-43.md:163:She had started it in the dairy week. Not that night; the night after, when she could not sleep for thinking about three carters and a road with four days of stamps on it and then none. She had thought then, lying on her back in the dark, about what she actually owned. Not the program. The program was Rooke's, and the east hall was the house's, and the red book belonged to a river academy and was only lent. The figure on the steward's sheet was hers, but it was hers the way a room is yours when somebody else holds the key; it meant something because a hall's seal was on it, and it would go on meaning something exactly as far as that seal was honoured.
