editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6630:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:12:- **Book 4 runs:** the final Greyvane term (≈5 months; Karis's find in week 3, the Edran rematch in week 20, Quenna in week 21, Prynn in week 22) → four days on the road → arrival at Halcenvane (five months and nine days after the ruling) → the season → **the eleventh of Sowing (Cael turns sixteen)** → the inspection, **the twelfth to the twenty-third of Reaping** (Copper final the 19th; semester evaluation the 20th; interview the 21st; departure the 23rd; file returned the 24th; quarterly drafted the 26th; corridor warning the 27th) → the first week of the month after Reaping (Lira's Arbiter evaluation) → term close → twelve-week recess (Book 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6707:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:584:- Lira's deep hip strain from the slide onto Fiske's slick (her foundry tallow-floor skill, new canon); four days off the hip; she fights the final on it. Vastin named at the reading ('Archmarshal Vastin'); NO stated age. Karis's slate draws the three columns (the insight and Log are Cael's). The hall-three slip is known only to Brom and Cael; the wing observer at the rail read nothing. Withrow's grain-store story (one Archmarshal-attended inspection in her twenty years). Gwen's aunt's dinner story (Gwen = placeholder, #11). Bracken 'he'.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6733:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:739:| **d177 (Fifth-day)** | **the thirteenth** | Cael's dawn stake. Lira off the stick (her four days end; six days to the final). **Vastin reads the filings before the first bell** (nine minutes, no mark) and tells the counsel he will sit the fifteenth. Records sittings on the provision's paper (registrar's boxes across at the second bell; a wing box at the fourth). Karis barred until the fifteenth. Ilsev crosses the walk before the third bell. Coursework on the day. Lira and Karis walk the yard. After the fourth bell, in rain: **Havel's inch**. Sixth bell: **fifth-line bout**, the Archmarshal from after the first call to the start of the fourth; supper thresholds with Brom. Night: Brom on the stair; bed at the eighth bell |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6771:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:935:| d187 | First-day | the 23rd | Departure in light rain; Ilsev at the steps; Havel's sixteen seals; Bracken countersigns. Lira's four days off the hip end (fourth bell); Cael's three days end that night. The Log ("Confused systems ask. This one checks.") |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6823:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:91:The first day of the qualifying year is day 0 (convocation), after a recess of twelve weeks and four days. No season is named anywhere in this book; weather words only; no month order, month length or cross-month day count is ever stated (OWNER #35, #36.4, #37 O1). Halcenvane's weekdays are the office's First-day … Seventh-day; English names appear only inside Daeva's window at Norhold (#37 O4). The first meet falls about five weeks in, the second about three weeks after it, the third "eleven weeks" after Seln's counter sentence, and the fourth at the year's turn in the deep cold; the road to Norhold runs seventeen days with the melt under the wheels; the tournament runs about three weeks with a rest day at its midpoint (the birthday: seventeen, the eleventh of Sowing by default, never beside a season word; OWNER #35 may move it to "the third of Reaping"). The road home is seventeen days. See `BOOK_MAP.md` §6. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6864:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:470:- Cael vs the grappler foreman (a Stone Path): one hand on him; Compression banked at contact; the LEFT shoulder-seam wrenched, four days (d83–d86); Rooke to look at it on the road. The RIGHT shoulder stays Pressure's private cost. Fenmark's third-form gap is on the LEFT foot (the gap Lira named at fourteen; the drill book carries her name on that foot). Lira: 'The moment was three years of work, and I already had it.' (year counts NOT incremented). The equipment mistress unnamed. Auremont is NOT the banner-holder. Zerin's and Marek's sheets: 'She's faster than me right now.' / 'The dangerous direction.' — protected item 38 'This one's been mispriced too.' with Brom's referent ('Every one of us priced below what we fight like').
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:6981:    31	- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:7010:   139	**Two hard rules for every window:** (1) **No member of Teague's crew is named, ever**, including in Teague's own head. Book 8 kills "the young one" at the pass and says his name once without entering it. Teague thinks of his people as the spear, the bow, the boy and the healer, which is how a captain counts. (2) **Oryn's holds stay unnamed** except Oxhollow, Thornwater and Millrace. In her head they are what they owe her or what is there: the hold with the child; the hold that gave the coat; the fourth, four days on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.stdout.log:7161:   319	- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
