editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/listening-proof.stdout.log:8862:**Two hard rules for every window:** (1) **No member of Teague's crew is named, ever**, including in Teague's own head. Book 8 kills "the young one" at the pass and says his name once without entering it. Teague thinks of his people as the spear, the bow, the boy and the healer, which is how a captain counts. (2) **Oryn's holds stay unnamed** except Oxhollow, Thornwater and Millrace. In her head they are what they owe her or what is there: the hold with the child; the hold that gave the coat; the fourth, four days on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-07.md:355:He had no word to give them, for a man did not speak to a bottom line that had cost him nothing. If they were what four lines said, then the board would put them across his road before the snow, and there would be something to say then, and something to price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-58.md:91:"Good." She put the great boot down whole, and the next. "She'd have answered you, and then she'd have had to carry having answered for four days through a gap. I thought that you'd know that. I wasn't sure of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:156:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`) and the coordinator's ten audit fixes. Facts changed: Teague knows only that the healer was late, not why, and cannot set his lost day against the five; Brom's older ash wedge was not lost and lies with the three boxes; Oryn's sum now reads whole on the 99th, the long reading on the 100th at the earliest, four days of work at Thornwater's table beyond her stop and one day put on the route; Seln asks leave to go ahead and leaves scratched pebbles for word, and finds a clawless footmark at the first seep; Oryn washes her hands before she kneels, and checks her hands on Brom's wrist in the middle of the first reading; the ankle is asked for from the mule's back on the morning of the 82nd; chapter 18 has three scenes. Word counts, metrics, line numbers and flags elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the movement now stands at 41,346 words.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:162:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:172:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken". **Her sum (her window, the 92nd):** whole on the 99th by the rule, though her hands say sooner; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; her Thornwater stop ends on the 95th; she means to work four days more at Thornwater's table and has put one day on the route, for the reading. She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record. She told Teague on the hill only that she was late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/review-cold.stdout.log:617:There was no moon, and the cloud had not lifted in four days. Past the stable passage the dark came down like a sack, and Cael stood in it at the top of the farm track with the others breathing round him and could not see his own hand.
