editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r3.stdout.log:1201:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:186:| 55 | ch7:211–215, 221–227 | "That's your sentence. You've been saying it since Greyvane… It's always been the people who failed and the paper that didn't."; "She looked at him for a while, in her slow way, three passes, the way she read an opponent's sheet the night before a bout… 'Bed… Four days of drafting, and she'll want us fed and quiet and out from under her feet.'"; Brom "stopped at its turn… 'Corridor,' he said, once more, to nobody, and went on up." | ch2:145–149 "That's your sentence. You've said it since Greyvane. The text holds when the people fail."; "She looked at him the way she had looked at Zerin's sheet — three reads, unhurried — and closed the drill-book, and said, 'Bed. Karis has four days of filing and she'll want us dumb and rested,'"; "stopped at the stair's turn, and said, to the room in general, 'Corridor,' once" | 0.55; the protected question and "Corridor." are allowed; the warden/provost/tournament triplet and Cael's new answer are the author's; the frames track |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r3.stdout.log:1376:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md-118-*Minute of the 40th: evaluation seat, to be called. Refusal of the 44th: fully constituted. Who sat down in those five chairs in four days, without asking this office for the file?*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r3.stdout.log:1486:books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-05.md:39:The four days ran on the office's ordinary clock. The certification dispute from the coastal district was resolved by a two-line advisory. The stations-office staffing note was annotated and returned. On the third day a junior evaluator from the northern district came up to the corner office with a difficult file — a Kindling record that did not match its practitioner's demonstrated architecture by a margin the junior found troubling — and Vastin reviewed it with him for an hour, patiently, the way he had reviewed such files for thirty years: the architecture was within tolerance; the record was sound; the margin was the ordinary variance of a young practitioner developing faster than his evaluators expected; continue observation. The junior thanked him and went down, reassured. Vastin sat afterward with the file's copy for longer than the file warranted, and could not have said why, and entered the not-saying in no ledger, because it was not yet a thing with a shape.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r3.stdout.log:1496:books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-05.md-49-The denial arrived in four days.
