editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:3694:He lay still on the scrubbed wood and looked at the underside of a turf roof. Nine things lay in him as quiet as he had ever known them; he had held them for eighty-four days, and it had become very like breathing. He could not tell what her fingers were reaching for. He knew only that none of the nine had stirred, and that if one had, he would have felt her feel it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:4359:- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
