editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5066:He lay still on the scrubbed wood and looked at the underside of a turf roof. Nine things lay in him as quiet as he had ever known them; he had held them for eighty-four days, and it had become very like breathing. He could not tell what her fingers were reaching for. He knew only that none of the nine had stirred, and that if one had, he would have felt her feel it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5214:So he would be whole four days after she had gone. She would be two gates on by then, and the round would not bring her back to Thornwater for twenty days more; and a crew off a board does not keep whole for twenty days. He would be on some other road, and as like as not broken in some other place.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5874:+So he would be whole four days after she had gone. She would be two gates on by then, and the round would not bring her back to Thornwater for twenty days more; and a crew off a board does not keep whole for twenty days. He would be on some other road, and as like as not broken in some other place.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6194:- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6236:| 18 | Tape; the lip; four days down; the route told (seven holds, twenty days); "The route is the only thing I own."; Oxhollow's table; the map paid; three readings; the two readings taught; three questions; "Thornwater's on my route in nine days…"; Teague at the ford: "The bench was a cart." (Ch7) | 81–84 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6266:2. **The compressed roads and recoveries put on the page (+38,000).** The source summarizes the six days in the fin's lee and on the mountain's lip (+4k); the four days down to Oxhollow (+4k); the six days Oxhollow→Lowmarch (+4k); days 60–69 at Lowmarch and the well on the south road (+8k); the two days stone→Thornwater with Lira flat-footed (+3k); Thornwater→Lowmarch in the first cold (+2k); the three-day bearing walk (+4k); and the six days from the fourth site home in first snow (+5k). Thornwater's three stays get texture as a place that becomes home (+4k). *Why:* the arc's freedom is made of walking and of places that feed them, and the source keeps cutting it to a sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6302:**Two hard rules for every window:** (1) **No member of Teague's crew is named, ever**, including in Teague's own head. Book 8 kills "the young one" at the pass and says his name once without entering it. Teague thinks of his people as the spear, the bow, the boy and the healer, which is how a captain counts. (2) **Oryn's holds stay unnamed** except Oxhollow, Thornwater and Millrace. In her head they are what they owe her or what is there: the hold with the child; the hold that gave the coat; the fourth, four days on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6482:- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
