editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:11397:55-- **Road times (prose, fixed):** Lowmarch ↔ Thornwater two days; Thornwater → the Fallow rise two days; Lowmarch → Oxhollow six days (north-west); Lowmarch → Millrace one day south on the Stair road; Millrace's fork → the Stair's line the same afternoon; the Stair → the Hall three days along the bearing; the Hall → the fork one day; the fork → the fourth site a day and a half; the fourth site → Lowmarch six days; the fourth site's gap → Thornwater four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:11493:395:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:11756:- **Oryn's sum (ch22:207–229), as it now stands on the page:** broken on the 78th; twenty-one days by the rule. Her hands say that he will be sound some days sooner, but she cannot read him, so she cannot know it, and she will not lift a tape on a guess: **whole on the 99th**. The long reading wants him whole and still and wants most of a day of her: **the 100th is the first morning she can run it.** She is at Thornwater on the 93rd (he is fifteen days from the break); her stop ends on the 95th. **"A week after she had gone" is now "four days after she had gone"**, and the round would not bring her back for twenty days. From the 95th to the 100th is five days. Four of them she can spend at Thornwater's own table as honest work, since the grain is moving and its bench will fill again; they make her late at six gates, and she knows whom she keeps waiting. The fifth, the day of the reading, mends nobody on her route and is owed by no hold: "If it was to be had, it must be added." **She put a day on the route.** The paragraphs on wanting are unchanged and now stand between the sum and the decision.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:11757:- This agrees with the day table (Thornwater 93; tape off 99; the reading on the 100th) and with the later lateness count (nine days late at Thornwater on the 104th means a stop that should have ended on the 95th). **For the coordinator:** Movement 4 has her walk the Fallow road with the crew on the 94th–98th instead of sitting at Thornwater's table. Her plan here is what she intends on the 92nd; she changes it at the gate on the 93rd ("You're a stop. I've added you."). If the ledger would sooner have her plan nothing for the four days, the paragraph beginning "She took it out of the round" can lose its second half without touching the last line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:11791:- **E, the four days.** I closed the sum by having her plan to work four days at Thornwater's table and add one, rather than add five or change "a day". That makes the page add up and keeps the packet's sentence; it also gives her a plan which Movement 4 overturns at the gate. Flagged above.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:11798:- **Oryn's sum:** whole on the 99th by the rule; the reading on the 100th at the earliest; her stop at Thornwater ends on the 95th; four days of work there and one day put on the route.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:11853:+Oryn's sum now states every needed term: the ribs break on day 78; twenty-one days makes Cael whole on day 99 by her rule; the deep reading can first run on day 100; her ordinary Thornwater stop would end on day 95; four intervening days can be honest table work; the reading day cannot, so `She put a day on the route.` The plan is consistent with the later packets **because it is her day-92 intention and is visibly changed at Thornwater's gate on day 93**. Movement 4 has her say `You're a stop. I've added you`, walk the Fallow road on days 94–95, and remain with the six through the Ring; Movement 5 returns them to Thornwater on day 99 and runs the deep reading on day 100. The BOOK_MAP table fixes those same days. Do **not** take the author's offered cut: removing the second half of `She took it out of the round` would erase the clean distinction between four days she initially counts as route work and the one day she knowingly adds, without improving downstream continuity.
