editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6521:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:74:**Calendar.** Matches the pending ledger block day for day: d168 courier/reading (Third-day, unit at the sixth bell); d170 Fifth-day board; d172 Seventh-day (Seln's requisition, Lira's room "If I win tomorrow"); d173 the ninth (file closed at the second bell; Lira–Fiske at the fourth bell); d174 the tenth (Brom–Merrick; "Nine days"); d175 the eleventh (slip; Brom "Nine days from now … three hours"; "Three nights ago" the cross — d172, correct; "two days ago" Merrick on the stair — d172, correct); d176 the twelfth (arrival at the fourth bell; close "seven days … eight"). Gwen's "on Third-day" for the next unit = d175, consistent with the weekly Third-day unit. Seln's bundle "would wait four days" from d172 = d176. Lira's "nine days" is counted from the tenth, as the ruling allows; the hip will be ten days old at the final, as the coordinator noted for M8. No Sowing date, no month order, no Sowing→Reaping count (#35). "A month back" for session fifteen (d141→d173 = 32 days) is fair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6733:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:157:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names. The interval log is day 0. Day 1 is First-day (dawn run and convocation; the instrument is dated this day). Day 2: the Silver floor and the reading room. Day 3: the counter and the north wall. Day 4: the docket at supper. Day 5, Fifth-day: wing three. Day 6, Sixth-day night: the honest floor. Day 7, Seventh-day: rest and Bracken's window. **Day 8, First-day: served**; the procedure runs that night into the small hours of day 9. **The answer is due at the seat in Ostrand by close of business on the twenty-second day.** Karis says the answer's shape will take four days. Brom's sitting is the last Fifth-day of the academic year.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6753:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:354:| 42–57 | ch7 | Redrafted whole. Changes, in order: <ul><li>The counsel: "I've looked tonight for the case where somebody turned these sections round to point at the man standing in the frame… This is new."</li><li>"Do you know the difference, in front of a seat, between a description and an evaluation?"</li><li>Bracken reads "flat"; the clerks' first-year joke ("the only page in the code nobody has ever had to stamp"); "imagined you" kept.</li><li>Withrow's morning after is rebuilt around the ferry, the guild master and the sealed file ("Kept, every page, perfectly safe, and nobody may open it"); "You can walk out of a town. You can't walk out of the post."; "Twice in my registry years I put my name to one. The first I'd sign again tomorrow… The second had a daughter."</li><li>The calendar: three silent marks read out by Karis ("The first. The eighth. The twenty-second."), with "in thirteen years I have never seen a seat take those three words back for anybody's lame horse".</li><li>The six slips are spoken as their words only, with one comment at the fifth.</li><li>The not-a-trick paragraph is now "Bracken would carry a paper like this. So would I… Look for the trick all night and you'll come up empty."</li><li>"the other choice has its own word in the docket, and the word is *fled*… I'll have bones on it in four days."</li><li>The stratum lead-in: "That clause is why you've never stood in a station since Denvash."</li><li>The note goes inside the front cover; the question mark: "She would answer it in her own time."</li><li>Seln's lamp: Cael "did not let himself guess what the man at the copying table was making".</li><li>Karis's instructions are cut to "Four days" and "Thank you for the tea".</li><li>The telling covers what moved the table, in a new order. Brom: "Then what's the answer for?" Cael's answer names the warden, provost and tournament himself; Lira: "And this time?… What if the people didn't fail this time?"; Lira leaves without the "Bed" line; Brom's second "Corridor." comes at the door.</li><li>Pole frame: "The entry was finished before the pen touched paper."</li><li>The prolepsis is trimmed to "It looked like the truth, because, as far as he could see from that window, it was."</li><li>The lamps go out by the hall's own count (the counter pair, the table's pairs from the far end, the press lamp last).</li></ul> |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6763:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:462:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names. Day 9 Second-day: drafting begins (four days to bones). Day 12 Fifth-day: bones. Day 13 night: the integrity section. Day 16: the counter. Two nights of Bracken's reading; the first rain; the weighing. **Day 19, Fifth-day: the answer goes down, three days inside the time** (due day 22). **Day 23: the seat's notice. Day 25, Fourth-day: Jent's conference; Withrow's office that evening.** Day 26 Fifth-day: board line; wing three. Day 27: the coats placed; the honest floor. **Day 30, Second-day: Lira's trial.** Day 31: the district docket's confirmation and the Velmere letter; opened the third evening (day 33). Day 35: Karis's budget; the frames days 35–38. Day 39: the annex convening. **Day 40, Fifth-day (the year's sixth): the first sitting.** **Day 42, Seventh-day: the month's close.** Lira's first meet off the hill is about four weeks away (Rooke's board). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6835:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:31:- **Cael vs the grappler foreman (~2,800):** the designed slow first exchange meets a real grappler. One hand gets on him. Compression stays banked at contact. The left shoulder-seam is wrenched and he scrambles; then he wins the long way. "Paid full price, first installment." The shoulder takes four days. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05: sided LEFT so it stays distinct from the right shoulder that pays the plate/Pressure (OWNER #36) and from Lira's Zerin "burst shoulder" in M6; audit C5.]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6844:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:12:- **Book 4 runs:** the final Greyvane term (≈5 months; Karis's find in week 3, the Edran rematch in week 20, Quenna in week 21, Prynn in week 22) → four days on the road → arrival at Halcenvane (five months and nine days after the ruling) → the season → **the eleventh of Sowing (Cael turns sixteen)** → the inspection, **the twelfth to the twenty-third of Reaping** (Copper final the 19th; semester evaluation the 20th; interview the 21st; departure the 23rd; file returned the 24th; quarterly drafted the 26th; corridor warning the 27th) → the first week of the month after Reaping (Lira's Arbiter evaluation) → term close → twelve-week recess (Book 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6858:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:91:The first day of the qualifying year is day 0 (convocation), after a recess of twelve weeks and four days. No season is named anywhere in this book; weather words only; no month order, month length or cross-month day count is ever stated (OWNER #35, #36.4, #37 O1). Halcenvane's weekdays are the office's First-day … Seventh-day; English names appear only inside Daeva's window at Norhold (#37 O4). The first meet falls about five weeks in, the second about three weeks after it, the third "eleven weeks" after Seln's counter sentence, and the fourth at the year's turn in the deep cold; the road to Norhold runs seventeen days with the melt under the wheels; the tournament runs about three weeks with a rest day at its midpoint (the birthday: seventeen, the eleventh of Sowing by default, never beside a season word; OWNER #35 may move it to "the third of Reaping"). The road home is seventeen days. See `BOOK_MAP.md` §6. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6890:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:74:**Calendar.** Matches the pending ledger block day for day: d168 courier/reading (Third-day, unit at the sixth bell); d170 Fifth-day board; d172 Seventh-day (Seln's requisition, Lira's room "If I win tomorrow"); d173 the ninth (file closed at the second bell; Lira–Fiske at the fourth bell); d174 the tenth (Brom–Merrick; "Nine days"); d175 the eleventh (slip; Brom "Nine days from now … three hours"; "Three nights ago" the cross — d172, correct; "two days ago" Merrick on the stair — d172, correct); d176 the twelfth (arrival at the fourth bell; close "seven days … eight"). Gwen's "on Third-day" for the next unit = d175, consistent with the weekly Third-day unit. Seln's bundle "would wait four days" from d172 = d176. Lira's "nine days" is counted from the tenth, as the ruling allows; the hip will be ten days old at the final, as the coordinator noted for M8. No Sowing date, no month order, no Sowing→Reaping count (#35). "A month back" for session fifteen (d141→d173 = 32 days) is fair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6894:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-001/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:19:| 5 | The First True Sentence | 5,275 | 5 | The toll board's nine lines; Brom pays; the barge horns; Karis's twenty thousand and the two Weighbridge Street offices; Halcenvane from mid-bridge; five months and nine days; fifteen. The bluff road's passing bays; watchers at the ferry and the road's foot; the gate clerk's four tracks. Intake: four desks for twelve; Brom nine minutes; Karis's eleven clauses; Lira's flag "goes on" to the queue and she makes the clerk write the dispatch date. Bracken: the stacks worked backward, Cael's catch, "never let a document… claim more than it proves", seventeen, the transcript at six silver marks, the record read three times, "It's the first one that's true.", two signatures, *94 min.*, Gault and the baseline, why twenty-two letters. The wall: carrel eleven; the grudge with a schedule; "Enrolled." … "I'd have paid more." |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6904:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-60.md:159:It was dated four days before. Hesk had not had his six pages. He could not have; they were still somewhere on the hill road, in Bracken's pouch. He had written off the broadsides, which reached the coast faster than any pouch. Then he had worked out which road the wagons would take, and which crossroads they would come to on which day, and sent the letter to meet them there. He had been right about all of it. Hesk's answers had always set out before the questions reached him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6914:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:292:2. **Lira's hip.** A deep strain from stopping on the slick in the long minute, "clicked once". Nothing on it for four days, then nine days to the final; "you'll fight on it". She climbs the tier against orders on d176.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6930:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:26:Checked every dated beat against the ledger's day-numbers and against each other. The recess: twelve weeks and four days, sixty-one sessions, nine letters, one dated change at the landing in the ninth week (ch1). The qualifying year: d0 convocation (First-day), d4 Fifth-day the filing and the counter, d5 Rooke signs Ephram's sheet, d8 the memorandum "four days after the courier", d9 the stair at a run, d10 Bracken's check, d11 Withrow signs, d12 the morning courier, d21 the fourteenth day crossed off, d16 Hesk's reply "the fourth day of the silence", d18 "the sixth evening" on the wall, d25 the card ("Thirteen days, Karis says", ch5:131, which is d12 to d25), d28 the map room "the first evening of the fifth week", d29 the mock ring, d30 "five days out" and "a little over three weeks" from the signing (ch4:153, d11 to d35), d33 the ferry, d34 the wool town, d35–36 the meet, d37 the ruling before noon, d38–39 half work, d45 Bracken on the stair, d46–52 a week west with frost on the fourth morning, d53 the mill town, d56 the yard-master, d57 the evaluation and "Variance is cheap", d59 the first pole at a coaching inn, d66 the circular "two days after the wagons got home", d67 the counter and the pouch "in two days", d69 the ferry, d77 the milestone and the silence, d78 the quarry town "at dusk on the tenth day", d81 the first meet day "eleven weeks" after d4 (ch15 and the ledger), the coat-rack "the end of the silence's fifth day", d83 the foreman and the costing "more than a fortnight ago" (d66), d84 the quarterly, d86 the waystation ("two days coming down", "another week" to the bluff, the circular at midday, the chancellor told "approximately four hours ago"), d93 the bluff on a Third-day evening, d97 the walking exchange "on the fourth morning", d101 "the second Fourth-day" on the speed line, d106 the wagons north with the carriage, d107 the confluence at dusk, d108–109 the meet, d110 the convenor, d112 the lamps on a First-day "two days later", d119 the cold term, d149 the reading room "a Third-day afternoon in the fifth week", the sixth week's letter, d186 Seln's report "the last Fifth-day", d187 the seedings, d188 the wall, "the next night" the melt, d190 departure on a Second-day. The road: day 3 the coast column, day 4 "downhill", day 6 the corner game, day 9 the flag "a week out", day 12 the five-arch bridge, day 14 the road sorting itself, day 17 the rise, day 18 the gate. Norhold: the second morning the likeness, the third evening Ephram's "pre-sold", the fourth Auremont, the fifth morning the orientation and the draw at dusk, Umber's eve, T1 "the first day of the new month", T2 the first rounds, T3 the two filings, T4 the trial rules and seat twelve, T5 Lira's quarterfinal and the deferral, T6 Ephram's exit, T7 the open warm-up, T8 Zerin and Brom's rematch, T9 Marek, Ilsev's form, Ivenne, the plaque "on the ninth day", T10 Karis's semifinal "the tenth day" and the crews, T11 the captain, T12 the cake ordered "the morning after your first bout", T13 the hired hall and Vastin by post road, T14 "the fourteenth day" and seat twelve filled "thirteen days" held, the night of seventeen, T15 the rest day, the fourth of Gault's four, the draw and the filing, T16 the trial, T17 Rhagen's news and "Twenty-first day, then, for third", "four mornings from now", T18 rain, the warehouse "on the second morning of the empty board", T19 the form "before dawn on the third day", Bracken's three troubles, the strip at dusk, the long table at the eighth bell, T20 the acceptance, the hearing at the fourth bell, the squall, Vastin's notice "the day after the filing" with departure "the morning after next", T21 the hill, the standings, the party and "three days from now", the midnight crews, T22 the shut hall, the ring "two days", T23 the fifth bell and the eve, T24 finals day, "two evenings ago" at the mast, the keeper's cap after "three weeks of mornings", T24–25 the panel, T25 the entry at dawn, the copy line, the return, the hour at the fourth bell, the pole, the rule, T26 the sixth guess "on the second morning", the closing at the second bell, the ledger "that evening", the pouch at the eighth bell, T27 Auremont's four words (as the M9 ledger corrects), road days 1, 3, 5, 9, 11 (Hesk's letter "dated four days before"), 12, 14, 17. Every Halcenvane weekday named falls where the ledger's arithmetic puts it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6990:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:74:3. §6's later dates (trial T12, filing T15, convening T16, ring conversation and third place T18, finals T20, panel T20–21, meeting T22, closing T23) shift by three or four days as a block, or the coordinator compresses the gaps; either way the coordinator, not the M7 author, should re-date §6 before M7 drafts. §6's "eleven days before the trial" for Zerin's semifinal was already inconsistent with its own T12 trial and should be dropped.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:7043:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:70:- **Timeline — ch5 l.131, "Nine days, Karis says, between the response going down and the card coming up."** The response left on the morning courier of a Sixth-day (ch4); the card arrived on a Fifth-day (ch5). On the seven-named-day week the text uses elsewhere (ch3: Fifth-day + four days = Second-day), Sixth-day to Fifth-day is six or thirteen days, never nine. Vastin's own count (advisory written, nine days of looking, card on the tenth) requires more than ten days plus transit each way, so thirteen is the number that fits both chapters. One word to change.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:7091:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-003/review-cold.md:19:**Which event I expect next.** Norhold. Specifically: Lira drawing Zerin in a semifinal and finding out whether "faster than me *right now*" holds; Cael meeting whoever has read the Auremont woman's page on his resets; Brom against Marek, the Copper who takes people apart at the joins. And the fourth meet, the threshold, and the shoulder having four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:7127:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/BOOK_MAP.md:237:- **[M6-redated 2026-10-05 — coordinator ruling; governs over the line above from T10 on.]** M6 (ch33) defers the exhibition ring by a west-tower notice on T5; the Copper final clears the main floor on T9 morning; the crews raise the ring on the night of T10, complete by dawn T11. Rooke's "four days … seven" (M5 ch32) is dead on the page and is not restated. Protected items 22–23 fix the order captain → duelist → rest day → trial ("Tomorrow I find out…"). New spine: **T11 Shield captain** (first Silver exhibition, main floor's ring). **T14 duelist** ("three days later"); **Vastin sits T14**, between the bouts' business; the chair was held T1–T13, so Seln's line reads "held for him for **thirteen** days" (not §10-protected). **T15 rest day = the birthday** (date still OWNER-pending #35; never beside a season word). **T16 team trial.** T17–T18 the empty board; **T19 filing**, the board at dusk; **T20 convening**; **T21 third place**, the ring rebuilt at midnight; T22 the ring "two days out"; T23 eve; **T24 finals day**; panel overnight T24–25; T25 the morning after and the meeting; **T26 closing.** Road home seventeen days. The office's "three weeks" (M5 ch29, ch32) stands as the round figure for the span; no later text states the tournament's length in days. Drop §6's "eleven days before the trial" for Zerin's semifinal (it was T8 against a T16 trial).
