o, d149 the reach "a quarter of the third hour", d150 the deferral, d154 the misfire "a little over ninety-six hours", d156 Brom's seventeenth, d158–161 the three leaks, d163 the moving half, d164 the coursework "on the fifteenth day", d167 Second-day the eleventh of Sowing with "sixteen days to the final" and the Log's "seventeen days", d168 Third-day the notice, d170 Fifth-day the schedule, d172 Seventh-day the compilation and Withrow's eleven minutes, d173 First-day the ninth of Reaping (file closed, Lira–Fiske), d174 the tenth (Brom–Merrick, "nine days"), d175 the slip, d176 Fourth-day the twelfth (arrival, "seven days… eight"), d177 the thirteenth ("six days"), d178 the fourteenth (hall three, the case home at the sixth bell, ledger day sixteen and twenty-nine since the stair), d179 the fifteenth ("Four days to the final. Five to the twentieth."), d183 the nineteenth (ledger day twenty-one), d184 the twentieth (day twenty-two, thirty-five since the stair), d185 the twenty-first, d186 "third morning of ice", d187 the twenty-third (Lira's four days end at the fourth bell, Cael's three that night), d188 the twenty-fourth ("ten days" after the fourteenth; the posting-house "eight days before" d196), d190 the twenty-sixth quarterly, d191 the twenty-seventh corridor, d196 the last unit, then the fifth, sixth, eighth, tenth, twelfth, thirteenth and fourteenth of the new month. The weekday scheme (First-day to Seventh-day) is consistent from d73 to the end. Hesk's reply on the twelfth to a letter posted the twenty-seventh is a fortnight's round trip to "the far end of the country", which the earlier books' post allows.
