editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log:8154:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md:71:Brom had come up behind them, slower. At the turn of the stair he stopped, and Cael, a step below, saw his right hand go to the left side of his coat, where the inside pocket was, and rest there flat over the cloth. There was a square cream envelope in that pocket with its dark red seal still whole. It had come up with the post four days ago, and he had turned it over once at the table and put it away unopened, and nobody had asked. Now an office in his own province kept an open book with a question in it about his family, and his grandmother could turn its pages whenever she liked.
