   196	
   197	"Nobody here has asked me for anything," said Vastin. "I noticed that on the landing, and I have been noticing it for two hours." He laid his left hand on the scrubbed wood. "So I will save you the asking. There are three things I will not do, and you should go home knowing which."
   198	
   199	He put one finger down on the table.
   200	
   201	"The first is verification." His eyes did not go to the case. "I want to. I have wanted to since the twenty-third pair. I could ride home and send for a frame and a station's own sheet and a fresh reading on any one of those forty children, and watch the case come true under my own hand, and sleep." The finger stayed where it was. "But there is no instrument in the Compact I could test it with that does not run on the thing it accuses. The frames are theirs. The sheets come up the same stair. The reading passes through the very function on that leaf before anybody writes it down. Whatever I measured would be a play put on for my benefit by the defendant." He was quiet a moment. "And a play of that kind has a cast. A girl's name on a request, or a junior's on an order. I will not put a child in a ledger so that an old man can feel sure."
   202	
   203	A second finger went down beside the first.
   204	
   205	"The second is a report. I have sworn to every report I ever made, and the oath is made to the office that receives it." He looked at the memoranda, at the nineteen seals. "That office is the one that wrote these. I should be swearing, in my best hand, to the man who forged them, and he would read it with great courtesy and enter it and thank me."
   206	
