editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-25.md:1:# Chapter 25 — The Slate Town
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-25.md:129:"No. I heard no order. I heard a count that came out one under, and I have never been able to leave such a thing alone."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:1:# Chapter 21 — The Road's Edge
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:183:"No. I saw you not ask." He drew a breath. "It was read with the one thing I've got that reads, and it came back with nothing. I don't mean that it's empty in there; I mean nothing came back. What I read with can feel a thing that moves, and whatever's in that place doesn't move, so the reading's got no way to say a word about it. I've been writing that nothing down for the better part of a year as if it were an answer. It wasn't one. It was only the thing I read with, telling me where it stops."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:195:"No. Nobody did. It was the one honest reading of you that the Compact ever held, and it said that I could not make one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:205:"No."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:253:"No. I know that." She shut the book over her thumb. "I never asked for it. I want that in there as well. I could have, and I'd have got it, and you'd have hated me for a month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:267:"No. I put one down beside it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-26.md:1:# Chapter 26 — The Iron Door
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-24.md:1:# Chapter 24 — Noon
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-24.md:167:"No."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-24.md:297:"No. I don't think he tells."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-24.md:317:"No. You're afraid that he'll look at them and say you're wrong."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-23.md:1:# Chapter 23 — Two Doors
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-22.md:1:# Chapter 22 — The Grey Bridge
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-22.md:229:"No. I was seventeen days late to your gate before the snow, and I'd a day there and no more; and then the cold shut the top road, and it's only now let me up it from this end."
