editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:397:- **S7 log:** "Ran the reading on myself again. Same nothing at the center. I think the reading can't do it — you can't measure a stillness with a thing that only feels movement. I need an instrument for what doesn't move. Karis says there's a man in Treswick who reads how things are built. Maybe that's the instrument. Maybe I'm about to hand a stranger the one question I've never let anyone hold. Tomorrow. The walls are close enough now to have a color." ("color" stands in the log, per ruling 19.) Also: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." / "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/pre-repair/chapter-22.md:69:He had come back inside a Compact wall for the first time since he walked down a bluff with a house's certificate in his coat; and he had come as the fifth part of a movement of a stranger's thumb. Nobody had asked what he was. No pen had been lifted. He went on up the paved slope beyond the arch with his box on his shoulders, and his heart going as it had gone on the lip of a cut, and found that he could not have said whether he was relieved or insulted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/recheck-prompt.md:23:- Confirm: every chapter within the three working ranges; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected; season-blind; no year count since the Kindling in narration; no possessive before "Path" in narration; no new proper noun; Cael never on the square or steps, never looking at the crown; Lira's paper unshown; Cleon's Path not shown; no fragment acquired; the still place never touched; consent explicit; no name of the four written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/pre-repair/chapter-23.md:87:There were strangers who came by right. He saw only one, a young man in travelling boots, who had the look of a courier. He took a folded paper from his coat without being asked, and the keeper with empty hands opened it and read it all, and read out a name and a district and a rank to his fellow; and the pen wrote for as long as it takes to say a line. The young man had his paper back and went up. He had been perfectly easy. He had been written in a book as a person is who has never had cause to mind it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/pre-repair/chapter-23.md:147:There was an uproar. He went on before it was settled, since a stranger who stands and watches children is marked in any town; but he carried it with him up the quay, and it was a little while before he could have said whether it had made him want to laugh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/pre-repair/chapter-23.md:263:The word was strange to Cael. He had stood on floors against a good many Paths, and had the pieces of ten of them in him, and he had never met that one on any list of bouts; it was not a thing that a person fought with, then. He lay and turned it over, and it told him nothing.
