editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/pre-repair/chapter-25.md:43:The room was hot, and smelled of tallow, and there was a young man in the corner who had been told to keep out of the way and could not find any. The woman on the bed had her eyes shut. She was perhaps twenty. She opened them when the pain let go of her, and looked at a strange square face in the lantern-light.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/pre-repair/chapter-25.md:177:Cael had her back in front of him, and a box on it, and above the box the back of her head. He could not see her face. He saw what her head did. As she came level with the board that hung from the second keeper's neck, where a line stood for every stranger who had walked through that gate today on his own paper, her chin turned toward it by the width of a finger.
